1
00:00:03,513 --> 00:00:04,381
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:00:04,402 --> 00:00:07,894
اَلْحَمْدُ لله  وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:08,469 --> 00:00:14,001
Lessons from the conversation between Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Rafea Bin Amr At-Taae(رافع بن عمروألطائ).

4
00:00:14,325 --> 00:00:17,072
Number one, speak to the people according to their level.

5
00:00:17,096 --> 00:00:18,617
حاطب الناس على قدر أقول

6
00:00:18,641 --> 00:00:23,152
This is a thief, he didn't go to school, he has no education background.

7
00:00:23,711 --> 00:00:25,847
Don't give him Bukhari(بخاريْ) and tell him memorize it

8
00:00:26,118 --> 00:00:30,751
and don't tell him you have to go on a Shariah(شريعة) course for a few years and study ilm(علم).

9
00:00:31,713 --> 00:00:33,834
People have different capabilities.

10
00:00:34,278 --> 00:00:37,595
Not everybody will become a great Shaikh(شيخ) and scholar,

11
00:00:38,928 --> 00:00:41,596
and not everybody will become an Imam(اِمَام), not everybody will be Daiyah(داعي)

12
00:00:41,803 --> 00:00:47,237
Imagine if Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه recited to this man Surah Al-Baqarah(سورة ألبقرة) and told him to memorize it,

13
00:00:47,968 --> 00:00:50,307
he could barely remember the five fingers, that's it.

14
00:00:51,856 --> 00:00:56,589
So the gangsters and brothers from that background, teach them take it easy with them.

15
00:00:57,182 --> 00:00:58,213
Take it easy with them.

16
00:00:59,609 --> 00:01:02,911
And Alhamdulillah(ألحمدلله), some of these brothers turned out to be wonderful brothers,

17
00:01:02,932 --> 00:01:04,305
when Allah guides them to the truth.

18
00:01:04,759 --> 00:01:09,477
The spirit that they have, is sometimes a spirit that you cannot find with a scholar.

19
00:01:10,626 --> 00:01:12,481
It happens that is Rizq(رزق) from Allah.

20
00:01:13,009 --> 00:01:18,506
I mean, Imam Ahmad Bin Hanbal(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْبن حنبل) once he heard somebody speaking about Bishral Haafie(بشرالحافي).

21
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:20,475
He said: He's not a scholar.

22
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:24,479
Bishral Haafie(بشرالحافي) wasn't a scholar in terms of memorizing a lot of Hadith(حديث).

23
00:01:24,503 --> 00:01:26,381
He's nothing to compare to Imam Ahmad Bin Hanbal(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْبن حنبل),

24
00:01:26,643 --> 00:01:28,249
but what did Imam Ahmad Bin Hanbal(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْبن حنبل) say;

25
00:01:29,034 --> 00:01:32,404
He already has the fruit of knowledge, Khashiat Allah(خشية الله).

26
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:36,121
He already has the fruit of knowledge which is the fear of Allah.

27
00:01:36,414 --> 00:01:37,438
What does that Ayah(آية) say?

28
00:01:37,652 --> 00:01:39,260
إِنَّمَا يَخْشَى اللَّهَ مِنْ عِبَادِهِ الْعُلَمَاءُ

29
00:01:39,284 --> 00:01:41,195
The ones who have fear of Allah are the scholars.

30
00:01:41,559 --> 00:01:44,699
So Allah is saying that the fruit of knowledge is the fear of Allah,

31
00:01:44,738 --> 00:01:47,869
there is no benefit in knowledge that doesn’t make you fear Allah.

32
00:01:48,645 --> 00:01:52,406
If you have all the knowledge in the world that you don't fear Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ it's worthless.

33
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:57,545
Ahmad Bin Hanbal(اَحْمَدْ بن حنبل) is saying this man already has the fruit of the knowledge.

34
00:01:57,706 --> 00:02:01,451
Therefore, really in his situation, knowledge, it's important,

35
00:02:01,647 --> 00:02:05,720
but he is a scholar in that sense, he has the fear of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

36
00:02:06,718 --> 00:02:09,784
So Rasool Allah ﷺ would speak to people differently.

37
00:02:12,262 --> 00:02:13,428
And the Sahabah(صحابه) understood that.

38
00:02:13,452 --> 00:02:17,062
Now Rasool Allah ﷺ when he is speaking to Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس), even though he was a child,

39
00:02:17,449 --> 00:02:19,508
but because he had the mind of a scholar,

40
00:02:19,645 --> 00:02:21,844
Rasool Allah ﷺ would speak to him on a very high level.

41
00:02:23,241 --> 00:02:25,406
While a Bedouin would come to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

42
00:02:25,482 --> 00:02:31,079
and he would give him very brief orders that are easy to remember.

43
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:33,881
So, you have to have Hikmah(حكمة) in Da'wah(دعوة)

44
00:02:33,905 --> 00:02:36,475
speak to the people according to their abilities.

45
00:02:36,954 --> 00:02:39,317
Number two, be honest,

46
00:02:40,238 --> 00:02:43,208
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه did not hold back anything.

47
00:02:43,248 --> 00:02:44,600
He said: Don't be a leader.

48
00:02:46,104 --> 00:02:49,297
And this is the first conversation he is having with the man he doesn't even know him well,

49
00:02:49,709 --> 00:02:50,517
don't be a leader.

50
00:02:51,006 --> 00:02:54,636
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) for some reason or another saw some things in this man,

51
00:02:54,987 --> 00:02:58,057
that do not befit position of authority.

52
00:02:58,378 --> 00:03:00,842
So he was very honest with him, told him don't be a leader.

53
00:03:01,167 --> 00:03:04,779
So also when you see something wrong in your brother, correct them.

54
00:03:04,881 --> 00:03:06,914
It's fine, it's okay, do it in a very nice way.

55
00:03:08,248 --> 00:03:10,184
FATTEH MAKKAH(فتح مكه), THE OPENING OF MAKKAH,

56
00:03:12,099 --> 00:03:15,681
Rasool Allah ﷺ had an agreement with the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), a truce,

57
00:03:16,021 --> 00:03:17,959
no war, that was in Sulhal Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبية).

58
00:03:20,395 --> 00:03:27,438
One  term in the agreement stated that if anyone wanted to enter into a coalition with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

59
00:03:27,478 --> 00:03:28,943
 they have the right to do so.

60
00:03:29,137 --> 00:03:33,875
And if anyone wanted to enter into coalition with Muhammadﷺ they have the right to do so.

61
00:03:37,001 --> 00:03:41,953
So according to the agreement, both sides are free to make alliances.

62
00:03:43,621 --> 00:03:46,898
Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) entered into an alliance with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

63
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:51,059
Khuza'a(خزاعه) entered into an alliance with Muhammadﷺ.

64
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:56,062
Khuza'a(خزاعه) had a special relationship with the grandfather of Muhammadﷺ

65
00:03:56,282 --> 00:03:59,567
and they carried on with the relationship with Muhammadﷺ,

66
00:03:59,591 --> 00:04:02,512
even though they were Mushrikeen(مشركين), but they wanted to be on his side.

67
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:08,417
They had an alliance with his grandfather and they wanted to continue the alliance of Muhammadﷺ,

68
00:04:08,659 --> 00:04:09,777
 even though they were Mushrikeen(مشركين).

69
00:04:11,759 --> 00:04:15,808
There was a feud between Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) and Khuza'a(خزاعه),

70
00:04:15,863 --> 00:04:17,652
they were at each other's necks.

71
00:04:18,825 --> 00:04:22,690
Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر), made an agreement, a secret agreement with some men in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

72
00:04:22,714 --> 00:04:24,392
that they provide them with weapons,

73
00:04:24,676 --> 00:04:28,229
and they make an ambush on Khuza'a(خزاعه) at night kill them and disappear.

74
00:04:28,793 --> 00:04:30,358
So some men of Khuza'a(خزاعه) were killed.

75
00:04:30,541 --> 00:04:33,517
Amr Bin Salim(عمروبن سالم), came to Muhammadﷺ,

76
00:04:33,818 --> 00:04:39,860
and he narrated lines of poetry, asking Muhammadﷺ to fulfill the agreement, and give him victory,

77
00:04:40,595 --> 00:04:46,031
that we have been betrayed by Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) and we've been betrayed by Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

78
00:04:46,285 --> 00:04:48,015
 Rasool Allah ﷺ immediately said:

79
00:04:48,039 --> 00:04:49,917
نُصرت يا عمرو بن سالم

80
00:04:49,941 --> 00:04:51,152
I will give you victory.

81
00:04:54,387 --> 00:05:00,933
Rasool Allah ﷺ went back home and he told Ayesha رضي الله عنها to prepare his luggage for battle,

82
00:05:00,996 --> 00:05:03,898
food and everything that he needed for this journey,

83
00:05:04,592 --> 00:05:07,940
but Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to make this expedition secret.

84
00:05:08,381 --> 00:05:10,905
Why? Because he wanted to avoid bloodshed in Makkah.

85
00:05:11,303 --> 00:05:15,710
So Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to mobilize his army and attack Makkah suddenly

86
00:05:16,079 --> 00:05:19,606
so that the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), only realized when it's too late for them to fight back,

87
00:05:20,366 --> 00:05:22,501
so that he can protect their blood.

88
00:05:23,081 --> 00:05:25,827
He doesn't want to give them time to prepare for war.

89
00:05:26,011 --> 00:05:30,258
So he wants to make his move, clandestine and quiet.

90
00:05:31,144 --> 00:05:33,108
So he told Ayesha(عائشه) to prepare everything for him.

91
00:05:33,604 --> 00:05:35,740
So she was grinding, some grain.

92
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:41,584
Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه, he came into the house and he saw that she was preparing luggage and all that,

93
00:05:41,910 --> 00:05:42,559
 he said:

94
00:05:43,449 --> 00:05:45,485
لعلى رسول الله يُريدو غزوة

95
00:05:45,895 --> 00:05:50,492
Is Rasool Allah ﷺ thinking about attacking an enemy?

96
00:05:51,452 --> 00:05:52,527
 She didn't respond.

97
00:05:53,678 --> 00:05:58,181
He told her, does he intend to fight the Romans?

98
00:05:58,355 --> 00:05:59,365
She didn't respond.

99
00:05:59,728 --> 00:06:02,121
Does he intend to fight the people of Najd(نجد)?

100
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:03,375
She didn't respond.

101
00:06:04,118 --> 00:06:05,861
Does he intend to fight the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)?

102
00:06:05,901 --> 00:06:06,990
She didn't respond.

103
00:06:08,041 --> 00:06:09,509
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ came in.

104
00:06:10,048 --> 00:06:15,117
So he asked him: O Messenger of Allah, are you planning for war?

105
00:06:15,346 --> 00:06:16,750
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes.

106
00:06:17,238 --> 00:06:18,816
He said: Is it with the Romans?

107
00:06:19,171 --> 00:06:20,305
Rasool Ullah said: No!

108
00:06:21,262 --> 00:06:22,612
Is it with the people of Najd(نجد).

109
00:06:22,837 --> 00:06:23,953
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No.

110
00:06:24,243 --> 00:06:26,368
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: Then is it the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)?

111
00:06:26,671 --> 00:06:28,115
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes!

112
00:06:28,579 --> 00:06:31,840
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) responded don't we have a truce between us.

113
00:06:32,087 --> 00:06:35,636
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Didn't you hear what they did to Bannu Ka'ab(بنوكعب).?

114
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:39,248
They have breached the agreement.

115
00:06:39,763 --> 00:06:44,447
Now, look at the conduct of Ayesha رضي الله عنها she kept quiet.

116
00:06:45,974 --> 00:06:47,948
To protect the secret of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

117
00:06:48,349 --> 00:06:51,518
Even with her father the closest man to Muhammadﷺ.

118
00:06:51,779 --> 00:06:54,103
Muhammadﷺ didn't keep his secret from Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), he told him,

119
00:06:54,529 --> 00:06:56,256
but Ayesha(عائشه) kept quite.

120
00:07:00,109 --> 00:07:01,923
The Battle of Hunain(حنين).

121
00:07:04,193 --> 00:07:08,906
Abu Qatadah Al-Ansari(أبوقتادةألأنصاري) from Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار). He said;

122
00:07:10,452 --> 00:07:15,036
I saw a Muslim, fighting with a Mushrik(مشرك).

123
00:07:15,931 --> 00:07:22,410
And there was another Mushrik(مشرك), who was trying to get around the Muslim and attack him from behind.

124
00:07:23,017 --> 00:07:25,519
So I attacked that Mushrik(مشرك) to protect my brother,

125
00:07:26,386 --> 00:07:30,557
when he saw me he lifted up his arm to hit me with his sword,

126
00:07:30,972 --> 00:07:34,406
but I was faster so I chopped off his arm.

127
00:07:35,019 --> 00:07:41,168
But then he hugged me, and he terrified me with his hug and then he became weaker.

128
00:07:41,662 --> 00:07:44,330
So I was able to kill him.

129
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:48,140
But then we retreated so I had to leave.

130
00:07:48,949 --> 00:07:50,519
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

131
00:07:50,649 --> 00:07:53,013
من قتل قتيلًا فله’ سلبه’

132
00:07:53,563 --> 00:07:58,074
If you killed anyone, then you can take their Salb(سلب),

133
00:07:58,099 --> 00:08:04,163
Salb(سلب) is whatever is with the fighter, there's a Ghanimah(غنيمه) and there is Salb(سلب).

134
00:08:04,188 --> 00:08:09,336
Ghanimah(غنيمه) is the booty of war, that’s all of the heavy equipments,

135
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:14,001
the camels, the horses, the wealth of the people that is booty.

136
00:08:14,769 --> 00:08:17,602
There is a different Hukum(حكم) for booty than there is for Salb(سلب).

137
00:08:17,627 --> 00:08:22,122
For booty the Ameer(أمير) divides it four fifths, goes to the fighters,

138
00:08:22,306 --> 00:08:26,696
and 1/5 is divided into five sections, that’s in the Ahkaam(أحكام) of Ghanaem(غنائم).

139
00:08:26,887 --> 00:08:29,349
But with As-Salb(ألسَّلب) it all goes to the fighter.

140
00:08:30,196 --> 00:08:37,176
So the personal weapons that are found on a dead soldier are taken by the one, who killed them.

141
00:08:37,453 --> 00:08:42,129
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said whoever killed someone, you take their Salb(سلب), you take their weapons.

142
00:08:42,253 --> 00:08:45,132
And there's a difference of opinion on what exactly is included in Salb(سلب).

143
00:08:45,268 --> 00:08:47,667
If you find some cash with them, their clothes,

144
00:08:48,050 --> 00:08:49,958
but that's something to look into in the books of Fiqh(فقه).

145
00:08:51,689 --> 00:08:56,083
Abu Qatadah(أبوقتادة) went and he found that there's nothing on this man, it was all taken

146
00:08:57,892 --> 00:09:01,693
and weapons are very expensive, and Abu Qatadah(أبوقتادة) was very poor.

147
00:09:03,693 --> 00:09:06,586
He went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and there were some people with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

148
00:09:06,610 --> 00:09:12,859
he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have killed this man, and I can't find his weapons.

149
00:09:15,069 --> 00:09:23,832
So one of the Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), who were there, he said: I am the one, who took the Salb(سلب),

150
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:25,667
I am the one, who took the weapons.

151
00:09:27,030 --> 00:09:35,751
So O Messenger of Allah, ask him to allow me to keep it.

152
00:09:36,845 --> 00:09:39,052
And that was the man whom Abu Qatadah(أبوقتادة) defended.

153
00:09:40,567 --> 00:09:48,628
Before Rasool Allah ﷺ responds, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) intervened and he said: No,

154
00:09:48,910 --> 00:09:52,771
In the Name of Allah, a weak bird from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

155
00:09:53,533 --> 00:09:58,501
is not going to take away the Salb(سلب) of a lion, of the lions of Allah,

156
00:09:58,636 --> 00:10:00,541
who's defending Allah and His Messenger.

157
00:10:02,351 --> 00:10:05,897
Now, the man who took the Salb(سلب) is from the Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), the people of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

158
00:10:06,556 --> 00:10:08,083
and Abu Qatadah(أبوقتادة) is from Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار),

159
00:10:08,229 --> 00:10:11,291
but Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) here is interfering and saying: The weak bird from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

160
00:10:11,650 --> 00:10:14,845
meaning you are the weak one, and he came to defend you,

161
00:10:14,992 --> 00:10:18,925
the weak bird of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) is not going to keep the weapons,

162
00:10:19,613 --> 00:10:23,861
but it should go to the lion of Allah, who is fighting to defend Allah and His Messenger.

163
00:10:25,539 --> 00:10:28,405
Rasool Allah ﷺ approved the Fatwa(فتوى) of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

164
00:10:28,485 --> 00:10:30,630
and he told the man, give him, his weapons back.

165
00:10:31,234 --> 00:10:33,722
The point to illustrate from the story is that

166
00:10:33,762 --> 00:10:38,344
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق)was at a level where he can give Fatwa(فتوى) in the presence of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

167
00:10:39,119 --> 00:10:42,250
where he can make a judgment in the court of Muhammadﷺ,

168
00:10:42,632 --> 00:10:45,753
he can make a ruling, when Rasool Allah ﷺ is right there.

169
00:10:46,976 --> 00:10:51,760
That is how intimate and close the relationship was because Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

170
00:10:52,430 --> 00:10:55,344
was drinking from the fountain of Prophethood for years and years,

171
00:10:55,637 --> 00:11:01,730
he has the Hikmah(حكمة) and wisdom, and Rasool Allah ﷺ approves, his ruling.

172
00:11:04,207 --> 00:11:06,989
Another thing worthy of mentioned in the Battle of Hunain(حنين),

173
00:11:07,013 --> 00:11:10,027
there were a lot of Ghanaem(غنائم), booties of war, alot,

174
00:11:11,841 --> 00:11:14,197
and there were many new Muslims in the army.

175
00:11:16,333 --> 00:11:20,269
Rasool Allah ﷺ gave these new Muslims the booty of war.

176
00:11:21,434 --> 00:11:26,909
And he withheld it from Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار) and the old Muslims.

177
00:11:28,673 --> 00:11:31,606
In order to draw these new Muslims closer to Islam,

178
00:11:32,814 --> 00:11:37,053
but still there was greed among these, some of these new converts.

179
00:11:38,027 --> 00:11:46,336
Al-Abbas Bin Mardaas(ألعباس بن مرداس), he was one of the chiefs of a clan, he made long poetry,

180
00:11:47,446 --> 00:11:53,461
 because he was upset, how come Rasool Allah ﷺ gives him equal to or less than Al-Aqra'a(ألأقراء) or Oyeyna(عيينة).

181
00:11:53,715 --> 00:11:57,168
Rasool Allah ﷺ gave them a certain amount,

182
00:11:58,025 --> 00:12:03,946
and Al-Abbas Bin Mardaas(ألعباس بن مرداس) didn't like that because he saw it as a matter of status.

183
00:12:05,734 --> 00:12:09,163
Whoever, is lowered on this day cannot be raised.

184
00:12:09,565 --> 00:12:14,724
You have lowered my status, and the Arabs will see that, that is my status and I cannot go up,

185
00:12:15,136 --> 00:12:17,301
so you have to give me equal to them.

186
00:12:18,039 --> 00:12:21,061
And there was a line of poetry. He says:

187
00:12:21,155 --> 00:12:25,574
جعلت نهبي ونهب العبيد، بين عيينه وأقراع

188
00:12:27,419 --> 00:12:30,816
When Rasool Allah ﷺ heard this poetry. He said: Go and cut his tongue.

189
00:12:31,351 --> 00:12:32,369
Not literally.

190
00:12:32,813 --> 00:12:36,397
But Rasool Allah ﷺ meant is give him, until he is quiet,

191
00:12:36,859 --> 00:12:42,881
cut his tongue means make him happy, so that his tongue wouldn't say something like that.

192
00:12:43,541 --> 00:12:45,454
Because poetry was powerful.

193
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:50,560
I mean, when we say that Ka'ab Ibn Ashraf(كعب إبن أشرف) was making poetry against the women of the Sahabah(صحابه),

194
00:12:50,931 --> 00:12:56,518
 poetry in Arabia had a greater influence on people, then a blockbuster movie would have today,

195
00:12:56,889 --> 00:13:03,205
or a front page article on The New York Times, or primetime TV with the BBC.

196
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:08,559
I mean poetry in with the Arabs was a very big deal, it was the media of the day.

197
00:13:10,017 --> 00:13:13,562
And there's an instance where one line of poetry,

198
00:13:14,425 --> 00:13:17,352
brought the end to the reputation of a tribe.

199
00:13:18,433 --> 00:13:20,222
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Go and cut his tongue,

200
00:13:20,246 --> 00:13:23,113
so they gave him and they gave him camels until he was happy.

201
00:13:24,515 --> 00:13:28,369
Later on, Rasool Allah ﷺ met with Al-Abbas(العباس), he met him,

202
00:13:28,639 --> 00:13:31,281
 And he said: Are you the one, who said:

203
00:13:32,163 --> 00:13:36,087
جعلت نهبي ونهب العبيد، بين أقراع و عيينه

204
00:13:37,655 --> 00:13:42,026
In the line of poetry, it is Uyeyna(عيينه) and then Al-Aqrah(ألأقراع).

205
00:13:43,532 --> 00:13:48,177
When Rasool Allah ﷺ narrated that line of poetry. He said,

206
00:13:48,595 --> 00:13:50,047
he switched the names.

207
00:13:50,485 --> 00:13:52,763
 He said: Al-Aqrah(ألأقراع) and Uyeyna(عيينه).

208
00:13:53,293 --> 00:13:57,195
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) corrected Rasool Allah ﷺ and he said: No! It's not

209
00:13:57,957 --> 00:14:00,477
Al-Aqrah(ألأقراع) and Uyeyna(عيينه), it is Uyeyna(عيينه) and Al-Aqrah(ألأقراع).

210
00:14:00,985 --> 00:14:02,996
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: It's the same thing.

211
00:14:03,592 --> 00:14:06,060
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) smiled and said:

212
00:14:06,785 --> 00:14:08,531
You are truly as Allah said:

213
00:14:08,555 --> 00:14:13,324
وَمَا عَلَّمْنَاهُ الشِّعْرَ وَمَا يَنبَغِي لَهُ ۚ إِنْ هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكْرٌ وَقُرْآنٌ مُّبِينٌ۝

214
00:14:13,712 --> 00:14:16,717
We have not taught him poetry and it's not appropriate for him.

215
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:20,472
It is only remembrance of Allah, and a manifest Book.

216
00:14:21,830 --> 00:14:24,934
I mean Rasool Allah ﷺ made this mistake in the poetry, it doesn't change the meaning,

217
00:14:25,055 --> 00:14:26,748
it's just the sequence of the names.

218
00:14:26,954 --> 00:14:30,278
So when Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) corrected it, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: It doesn't make a difference.

219
00:14:31,047 --> 00:14:32,942
To Rasool Allah ﷺ, it doesn't make a difference,

220
00:14:33,243 --> 00:14:36,584
but to the listeners of poetry, you have to follow the rules.

221
00:14:37,316 --> 00:14:40,000
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said: Yes! You're as Allah said:

222
00:14:40,025 --> 00:14:41,256
وَمَا عَلَّمْنَاهُ الشِّعْرَ

223
00:14:41,474 --> 00:14:46,181
We did not teach him poetry, and it's not appropriate for him, but it is Qur'an.

224
00:14:48,015 --> 00:14:51,866
In the siege of At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف) when the Muslims were laying siege to At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف),

225
00:14:52,750 --> 00:14:58,506
an arrow injured the son of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, Abdullah(عبدالله)

226
00:14:59,221 --> 00:15:04,361
and that injury was the cause of his death, but it was a long time after that it happened,

227
00:15:04,525 --> 00:15:07,248
he only died after Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

228
00:15:08,586 --> 00:15:10,831
When Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was Khalifah(خليفه).

229
00:15:11,728 --> 00:15:13,784
He received the delegation from At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف).

230
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:17,959
This was a long time after the incident happened of shooting the arrow,

231
00:15:18,455 --> 00:15:20,733
shooting the arrow happened in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

232
00:15:21,183 --> 00:15:24,199
his son died because of it, during the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

233
00:15:24,629 --> 00:15:26,913
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) retained the arrow, he kept it with him.

234
00:15:27,741 --> 00:15:29,807
It was the cause of the death of his son, Abdullah(عبدالله).

235
00:15:31,296 --> 00:15:36,360
When he received the delegation from At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف), coming to visit him as the Khalifah(خليفه),

236
00:15:36,646 --> 00:15:40,204
 he pulled out the arrow, and he said: Is any one of you know the source of this arrow.

237
00:15:40,902 --> 00:15:43,997
It happened that one of the men who were present,

238
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:49,727
he said: I am the one who prepared this arrow, I'm the one who sharpened it,

239
00:15:49,946 --> 00:15:53,673
I'm the one, who attach the feathers to it, and I'm the one who shot it.

240
00:15:55,564 --> 00:16:00,780
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: This is the arrow that killed my son Abdullah(عبدالله).

241
00:16:02,459 --> 00:16:05,478
What was the response of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), he lost his son.

242
00:16:06,412 --> 00:16:11,191
He said: So Praised be to Allah, who honored him, through you.

243
00:16:13,047 --> 00:16:18,398
And did not dishonor you and made you a Muslim

244
00:16:19,135 --> 00:16:21,067
and that is better for both of you.

245
00:16:21,931 --> 00:16:24,846
Allah honored my sons, through you, you are the one, who made him a Shaheed(شهيد).

246
00:16:26,885 --> 00:16:30,310
And Allah did not dishonor you, He made you a Muslim so it's good for you.

247
00:16:31,833 --> 00:16:37,606
And there's a narration that says, the two men, who love each other the most in Jannah(جنة),

248
00:16:39,723 --> 00:16:43,456
are the Kafir(كافر) who killed the Muslim, and then became a Muslim himself.

249
00:16:44,695 --> 00:16:46,636
They end up loving each other so much in Jannah(جنة).

250
00:16:47,171 --> 00:16:52,892
Because the martyr knows that this is the one, who killed me and gave me this status.

251
00:16:53,397 --> 00:16:57,316
And that person praised Allah that he did not, wasn't punished for that

252
00:16:57,340 --> 00:17:01,049
and he ended up becoming a muslim himself, so that's At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف).

253
00:17:03,117 --> 00:17:03,917
Tabook(تبوك),

254
00:17:05,488 --> 00:17:12,331
The Battle of Tabook(تبوك), was the first time Rasool Allah ﷺ by himself will go out and face the Romans,

255
00:17:12,621 --> 00:17:15,488
there was an initial encounter in the Battle of Mu'tah(مؤته),

256
00:17:16,197 --> 00:17:20,888
but this time Rasool Allah ﷺ wants to go, himself, and lead an army

257
00:17:21,305 --> 00:17:23,903
and make an incursion into the Roman Empire.

258
00:17:24,189 --> 00:17:28,718
So it was a very special event, it needed some special preparation,

259
00:17:29,210 --> 00:17:33,380
different than any other battle that Rasool Allah ﷺ participated in.

260
00:17:34,008 --> 00:17:38,551
And in this battle, he gave the great banner to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

261
00:17:40,289 --> 00:17:43,690
When the army marched out, and there were camping at night.

262
00:17:46,024 --> 00:17:49,428
This was a long journey so one of those nights they were out in the desert camping.

263
00:17:51,733 --> 00:17:55,902
So Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said: I saw a fire in the distance,

264
00:17:56,108 --> 00:17:58,048
so I wanted to go and see what was happening.

265
00:18:00,099 --> 00:18:07,266
He said: I went there and I found, Abdullah Ibn Abi Bajadain(عبدالله إبن أبي بجادين) dead.

266
00:18:08,583 --> 00:18:10,019
This is one of the companions of Rasool Ullah,

267
00:18:12,210 --> 00:18:15,455
and with him were Rasool Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر).

268
00:18:16,671 --> 00:18:19,592
And Rasool Allah ﷺ was in the grave.

269
00:18:20,416 --> 00:18:23,834
And he was telling, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) to lower the body of Abdullah(عبدالله).

270
00:18:24,682 --> 00:18:26,733
He said: Bring down your brother,

271
00:18:27,580 --> 00:18:33,156
and Rasool Allah ﷺ placed him with his own hands in the grave, and then he said:

272
00:18:33,942 --> 00:18:36,776
اللهم إني أمسيت عليه راضيً فرداعني

273
00:18:37,386 --> 00:18:41,469
O Allah! I am going to bed this night and I'm pleased with him

274
00:18:41,657 --> 00:18:43,360
so O, Allah be pleased with him.

275
00:18:43,922 --> 00:18:48,421
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said: I desire and wished that I was the one in that grave.

276
00:18:49,125 --> 00:18:51,454
To receive this Dua(دُعَا) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

277
00:18:51,704 --> 00:18:54,627
that I am pleased with him, so O Allah be pleased with him.

278
00:18:55,642 --> 00:18:58,337
Again it was Rasool Allah ﷺ Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر).

279
00:19:00,878 --> 00:19:04,437
It was very difficult time, hot in summer.

280
00:19:04,917 --> 00:19:09,858
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: It got to a level where we didn't have any water left,

281
00:19:10,198 --> 00:19:16,494
so we would slaughter our camels and drink whatever is in their stomachs

282
00:19:17,205 --> 00:19:20,754
the digested food, they will drink that that's how thirsty they were.

283
00:19:21,034 --> 00:19:23,323
And then he said, and we take whatever is left and

284
00:19:23,347 --> 00:19:25,425
we put we will put it on our bodies to cool down.

285
00:19:26,702 --> 00:19:29,683
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه when to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said:

286
00:19:29,707 --> 00:19:33,186
O Messenger of Allah, your Dua(دُعَا) is accepted, make Dua(دُعَا) for us.

287
00:19:34,603 --> 00:19:36,310
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked Abu Bakr(أبوبكر)

288
00:19:36,517 --> 00:19:37,646
أوَ تحب ذالك؟

289
00:19:38,197 --> 00:19:40,611
Is that something you want, you love that?

290
00:19:40,794 --> 00:19:41,992
Meaning I will do it for you.

291
00:19:42,474 --> 00:19:43,500
Is that what you want?

292
00:19:43,667 --> 00:19:45,175
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said: Yes!

293
00:19:45,422 --> 00:19:48,651
Rasool Allah ﷺ made Dua(دُعَا), the narrative of the Hadith(حديث) says:

294
00:19:48,936 --> 00:19:53,318
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not bring his hands down, until the clouds are above our heads.

295
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:56,747
In the spending in the Battle of the Tabook(تبوك)

296
00:19:56,772 --> 00:19:58,849
and the spending in the Battle of Tabook(تبوك) was special.

297
00:19:59,459 --> 00:20:02,608
That is when Rasool Allah ﷺ praised Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان)

298
00:20:02,633 --> 00:20:04,580
and we talked about that in our first session.

299
00:20:05,342 --> 00:20:06,407
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

300
00:20:06,431 --> 00:20:09,938
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was asking for donations for the preparation of the Army.

301
00:20:10,158 --> 00:20:11,497
صادف ذالك عندي مالي

302
00:20:11,584 --> 00:20:13,979
At that time, I had some money.

303
00:20:14,685 --> 00:20:20,113
So I told myself today I am going to be ahead of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

304
00:20:20,282 --> 00:20:23,284
if I'm ever going to be ahead of him, this is my chance.

305
00:20:24,226 --> 00:20:26,316
So he said: I carried with me half of my wealth

306
00:20:26,337 --> 00:20:28,468
and I went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and I gave it to him.

307
00:20:28,850 --> 00:20:30,957
He said: O Umar(عُمَر)! What have you left for your family?

308
00:20:31,306 --> 00:20:34,035
He said: I left them, half of my wealth.

309
00:20:36,015 --> 00:20:37,022
And then Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) came

310
00:20:38,565 --> 00:20:40,103
and he gave his money to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

311
00:20:40,127 --> 00:20:43,121
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked him: What have you left for your family.

312
00:20:43,495 --> 00:20:45,280
He said: I've left them Allah and His Messenger.

313
00:20:45,877 --> 00:20:47,211
He brought all of his wealth!

314
00:20:47,357 --> 00:20:50,861
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: I will never try again to compete with you.

315
00:20:52,005 --> 00:20:55,165
I'm never going to try to be ahead of you, He can't!

316
00:20:56,623 --> 00:20:57,846
And this is in Tabook(تبوك).

317
00:20:58,194 --> 00:21:03,913
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) persisted in his attempts all the way until the Battle of Tabook(تبوك)

318
00:21:03,967 --> 00:21:06,880
 but then he said: I am not gonna do it again Khalas(خلاص), I give up.

319
00:21:09,943 --> 00:21:10,669
AL-HAJJ(حَجْ),

320
00:21:10,959 --> 00:21:14,517
In Ninth year of Hijrah(هجرة), which is Hajja Tul Widdah(حجةالوداع)

321
00:21:15,271 --> 00:21:20,573
Before Hajja Tul Widdah(حجةالوداع) the year before Hajja Tul Widdah(حجةالوداع)

322
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:24,589
Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to lead the Hajj(حَجْ).

323
00:21:26,462 --> 00:21:27,810
He appointed Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to lead the Hajj(حَجْ).

324
00:21:27,850 --> 00:21:30,256
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to make Hajj(حَجْ) himself, but he said:

325
00:21:30,651 --> 00:21:32,294
It's not appropriate for me to make Hajj(حَجْ)

326
00:21:32,319 --> 00:21:34,770
when there are people who are going around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) naked.

327
00:21:36,570 --> 00:21:41,360
There was a belief among the Arabs that only the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are pure

328
00:21:41,479 --> 00:21:43,312
therefore they can make Tawaf(طواف) with their clothes.

329
00:21:43,775 --> 00:21:48,020
But because we commit sins, our clothes are impure so we have to take them off

330
00:21:48,650 --> 00:21:51,615
and they would make Tawaf(طواف) naked.

331
00:21:51,912 --> 00:21:53,918
Now, not every one of them would do that.

332
00:21:54,408 --> 00:21:57,275
They used to believe that if they want to make Tawaf(طواف) around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

333
00:21:57,296 --> 00:22:00,633
they have to borrow the clothes or buy the clothes of somebody from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

334
00:22:01,262 --> 00:22:02,619
Because they are the pure people.

335
00:22:03,286 --> 00:22:07,309
So if they would have money they would buy clothes, whoever doesn't have money, they would make Tawaf(طواف) naked.

336
00:22:08,157 --> 00:22:13,205
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said: It's not appropriate for me to make Tawaf(طواف) when this is going on.

337
00:22:13,536 --> 00:22:16,465
 So he told Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه to lead, Al-Hajj(ألحَجْ).

338
00:22:16,671 --> 00:22:21,864
And this is an indication that sometimes a leader needs to stay away from things

339
00:22:22,383 --> 00:22:24,112
that are allowed for the rest of the Ummah(امة).

340
00:22:24,734 --> 00:22:26,808
Because of that important position of leadership.

341
00:22:27,358 --> 00:22:31,511
Rasool Allah ﷺ didn't do it himself, but he allowed the Muslims to go and make Hajj(حَجْ).

342
00:22:32,125 --> 00:22:40,518
So the leader needs to follow stricter rules than the layman, to uphold a higher standard.

343
00:22:41,271 --> 00:22:42,812
Anyway, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) left.

344
00:22:43,248 --> 00:22:48,691
When he left, Rasool Allah ﷺ received the revelation.

345
00:22:48,773 --> 00:22:50,581
The first Ayaat(آيات) from Surah At-Taubah(سورة ألتوبة)

346
00:22:50,990 --> 00:22:55,975
which are announcing the end of the agreement between Rasool Allah ﷺ and Kuffar(كفار)

347
00:22:56,221 --> 00:22:59,214
and the end of the era of Shirk(شرك) in Arabia, it's over.

348
00:22:59,858 --> 00:23:04,156
Now, it's either Islam or the sword, no other choice.

349
00:23:04,949 --> 00:23:10,943
 So Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) to take his camel Al-Adba'a(ألعضباء), and to go fast,

350
00:23:11,492 --> 00:23:13,593
and follow Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

351
00:23:13,836 --> 00:23:18,788
and to convey to the people, to recite the Ayaat(آيات) of Surah Al-Bara'a(سورة ألبراء) to the people.

352
00:23:19,135 --> 00:23:21,227
 And it's the only Surah(سورة) in Qur'an that doesn’t start with,

353
00:23:21,267 --> 00:23:22,412
 بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم

354
00:23:23,046 --> 00:23:24,775
Because it's an announcement of war

355
00:23:24,989 --> 00:23:27,891
so it doesn't start with the Merciful and the Beneficent.

356
00:23:29,217 --> 00:23:35,540
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) went very fast, until he reached Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in Dhul Khalifah(ذوالخليفه).

357
00:23:36,701 --> 00:23:40,857
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه saw him riding the camel of Rasool Allah ﷺ, he told him:

358
00:23:41,023 --> 00:23:42,128
 أميرٌ أمَّعمور

359
00:23:42,923 --> 00:23:45,532
Are you leading or are you a follower.?

360
00:23:45,851 --> 00:23:46,652
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said:

361
00:23:46,716 --> 00:23:47,301
بل معمور

362
00:23:47,358 --> 00:23:48,043
I'm a follower

363
00:23:49,122 --> 00:23:52,517
because Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) thought that maybe Ali(علي) is a new leader of Al-Hajj(حَجْ).

364
00:23:52,884 --> 00:23:54,214
He said: No! I am a follower.

365
00:23:55,224 --> 00:23:56,916
 So they went to Makkah

366
00:23:57,240 --> 00:24:02,135
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) would take the people in the different positions of Hajj(حَجْ) in the different rituals,

367
00:24:02,444 --> 00:24:05,357
 and Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) would follow him wherever he goes,

368
00:24:05,674 --> 00:24:08,423
 and would recite the Ayaat(آيات) of Bara'a(برآء) on everyone

369
00:24:08,579 --> 00:24:10,429
and then he would announce four things.

370
00:24:10,752 --> 00:24:13,244
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him to tell the people the following:

371
00:24:13,597 --> 00:24:14,268
 Number one;

372
00:24:14,313 --> 00:24:16,789
لا يدخل الّجنة إلَّا مؤمن

373
00:24:17,495 --> 00:24:20,535
No one will enter Jannah(جنة), unless they're believers.

374
00:24:21,141 --> 00:24:21,917
Number two

375
00:24:22,118 --> 00:24:23,746
ولا يطوفو بالبيت عريان

376
00:24:24,016 --> 00:24:26,722
No one should make the Tawaf(طواف) around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) - if they're naked.

377
00:24:27,052 --> 00:24:27,719
Number three,

378
00:24:28,037 --> 00:24:31,920
ومن كان بينه و بين رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم عهدُ وعهدٌ على مدة

379
00:24:32,260 --> 00:24:36,666
And if you have a peace agreement between you and Muhammadﷺ

380
00:24:36,893 --> 00:24:41,078
then it ends at the end of the term, and it won't be renewed.

381
00:24:41,439 --> 00:24:42,246
And finally

382
00:24:42,399 --> 00:24:44,646
ولا يحج بعد العام مشرك

383
00:24:45,325 --> 00:24:48,005
And no Mushrik(مشرك) shall make Hajj(حَجْ) after this year.

384
00:24:48,161 --> 00:24:53,863
So, the era of Shirk(شرك) is over with, Shirk(شرك) is now behind our backs.

385
00:24:54,138 --> 00:24:56,391
So Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) made these terms clear

386
00:24:56,628 --> 00:25:01,000
as a preparation for Rasool Allah ﷺ coming the next year and leading the Hajj(حَجْ)

387
00:25:01,249 --> 00:25:02,526
with no Shirk(شرك) around.

388
00:25:02,742 --> 00:25:04,568
So, Makkah will now be purified.

389
00:25:05,269 --> 00:25:07,422
Now notice the clear instructions

390
00:25:07,629 --> 00:25:08,883
لا يدخل الّجنة إلَّا مؤمن

391
00:25:09,536 --> 00:25:11,779
That only the believers will enter into Jannah(جنة).

392
00:25:12,523 --> 00:25:12,927
Numbers two;

393
00:25:13,003 --> 00:25:14,399
ولا يطوفو بالبيت عريان

394
00:25:14,464 --> 00:25:17,112
No more nakedness around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), to purify Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

395
00:25:17,487 --> 00:25:19,311
and then the truce agreements.

396
00:25:19,656 --> 00:25:23,437
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not breach any agreement he said: You have four months

397
00:25:24,211 --> 00:25:29,174
and after that, all agreements are terminated, and it's either Islam or the sword.

398
00:25:30,962 --> 00:25:35,219
So this is in Hajjat(حجة) Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

399
00:25:36,395 --> 00:25:40,740
In Hajjal Waddah(حج الوداع) and this is the only Hajj(حَجْ), that Rasool Allah ﷺ did

400
00:25:41,728 --> 00:25:47,085
Hajjat-Tul-Widaa(حجة الوداع), the only thing that I would mention here is an incident.

401
00:25:47,140 --> 00:25:50,277
Asma(أسماء) is narrating this she said:

402
00:25:50,523 --> 00:25:55,210
Rasool Allah ﷺ was sitting with Ayesha(عائشه) sitting next to him and

403
00:25:55,741 --> 00:26:00,010
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is waiting for his servant to bring back his camel

404
00:26:01,171 --> 00:26:03,277
and is waiting and waiting and the servant was late

405
00:26:03,309 --> 00:26:07,308
and then suddenly here comes the servant, without the camel.

406
00:26:09,210 --> 00:26:12,168
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) told him: Where's the camel, he said I lost it yesterday

407
00:26:12,594 --> 00:26:13,201
What?

408
00:26:14,045 --> 00:26:15,835
He attacked him and he started beating him.

409
00:26:16,442 --> 00:26:19,778
So Rasool Allah ﷺ smiled and he said: Look at what this Muhram(مُحرم) man is doing

410
00:26:20,275 --> 00:26:21,368
he is in the State of Ehraam(إحرام).

411
00:26:22,544 --> 00:26:24,780
But that was the only camel that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) had

412
00:26:24,804 --> 00:26:27,875
so he was very upset that his servants lost his camel.

413
00:26:29,637 --> 00:26:35,269
So, this is the end of the Jihad(جهاد) of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

414
00:26:35,734 --> 00:26:37,692
We'll move on to the next stage.

415
00:26:38,097 --> 00:26:43,571
In sha Allah Ho Ta'ala(إن شاء الله تعالى) this session we'll go through some events

416
00:26:44,091 --> 00:26:46,986
involving Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in Madina.

417
00:26:48,388 --> 00:26:56,186
We talked in the previous session about the participation of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in the Ghazawaat(غزوات).

418
00:26:56,857 --> 00:26:59,456
So now we'll talk about the non Ghazawaat(غزوات)

419
00:27:00,132 --> 00:27:04,595
events that happened with As-Siddique رضوان الله عليه.

420
00:27:06,903 --> 00:27:11,578
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would protect the secret of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

421
00:27:14,175 --> 00:27:18,490
The daughter of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه, Hafsa(حفصه)

422
00:27:19,495 --> 00:27:26,357
was married to one of the Sahabah(صحابه), who has fought in the Battle of Badr(بدر) later on, he died.

423
00:27:27,064 --> 00:27:33,103
 So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه wanted his daughter to marry from the best.

424
00:27:34,105 --> 00:27:37,548
 So he went to Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) and he offered his daughter to him.

425
00:27:38,862 --> 00:27:43,525
He told Uthman Ibn Affan رضي الله عنه do you want to marry my daughter Hafsa(حفصه)?

426
00:27:45,326 --> 00:27:48,152
Uthman Ibn Affan رضي الله عنه said: Let me think about it.

427
00:27:49,011 --> 00:27:51,687
He later on came back and said;

428
00:27:52,302 --> 00:27:54,994
قد بدالي ألَّا تزوجه يوم هذا

429
00:27:56,045 --> 00:27:59,540
I've decided that I don't want to marry at this particular time

430
00:27:59,880 --> 00:28:01,561
I'm not interested in marriage now.

431
00:28:03,581 --> 00:28:08,598
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه might have disliked that a little bit

432
00:28:08,806 --> 00:28:12,751
so he went to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

433
00:28:13,418 --> 00:28:18,924
And he told him I'm offering you my daughter, if you want to marry her.

434
00:28:20,045 --> 00:28:24,210
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه did not respond, didn't say anything.

435
00:28:25,574 --> 00:28:30,309
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: I was even more upset with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) than I was with Uthman(عثمان).

436
00:28:31,090 --> 00:28:33,890
At least Uthman(عثمان) came and gave me an answer

437
00:28:33,914 --> 00:28:36,602
even though it was a no answer, but at least he gave me an answer.

438
00:28:39,700 --> 00:28:41,851
But Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was silent

439
00:28:42,527 --> 00:28:44,780
I offer my daughter to him, he doesn't give me an answer.

440
00:28:48,628 --> 00:28:53,705
A few days later, Rasool Allah ﷺ, marries Hafsa(حفصه).

441
00:28:56,569 --> 00:29:01,058
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه after the marriage he came to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

442
00:29:01,082 --> 00:29:06,534
and said: I think that you were upset with me because I didn't give you an answer

443
00:29:06,897 --> 00:29:08,762
He said: Yes! I was upset with you.

444
00:29:09,404 --> 00:29:11,150
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

445
00:29:11,218 --> 00:29:18,347
The reason why I didn't respond back is, because I heard Rasool Allah ﷺ mention her

446
00:29:18,898 --> 00:29:23,167
and I wasn't going to be the one who would disclose the secret of Rasool Allah ﷺ

447
00:29:23,890 --> 00:29:26,254
and if he did not marry her, I would have married her.

448
00:29:28,641 --> 00:29:33,929
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: I felt that Rasool Allah ﷺ by mentioning her name was interested in her.

449
00:29:35,467 --> 00:29:38,291
And that's why I kept quiet to wait and see what will happen?

450
00:29:38,315 --> 00:29:41,339
If Rasool Allah ﷺ does not marry her, I would have married her.

451
00:29:42,570 --> 00:29:47,646
But I am not going to be the one, who will disclose the secret of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

452
00:29:49,744 --> 00:29:58,992
Rasool Ullah صلوات الله ولسلام عليه , wanted to have a relationship, a marriage relationship

453
00:29:59,520 --> 00:30:02,299
with the fourth Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

454
00:30:03,256 --> 00:30:06,500
So you find that he married the daughter of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق)

455
00:30:06,903 --> 00:30:09,849
and he married the daughter of Umar Al-Farooq(عُمَرألفاروق)

456
00:30:10,962 --> 00:30:14,574
and then he married two of his daughters to Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان)

457
00:30:14,907 --> 00:30:18,128
first he married him one and then when she passed away he married him the other.

458
00:30:19,273 --> 00:30:21,017
And there is a statement that says;

459
00:30:21,127 --> 00:30:23,195
Allah Ho Alam(الله أعلم) how strong the narration is but

460
00:30:23,660 --> 00:30:27,207
if I had 99 daughters, I would marry them to Uthman(عثمان)

461
00:30:27,882 --> 00:30:29,957
if one of them die, I will keep on marrying him.

462
00:30:30,985 --> 00:30:35,208
That is how much love Rasool Allah ﷺ had for Uthman Ibn Affan رضي الله عنه

463
00:30:35,513 --> 00:30:38,939
and then he married his daughter, Fatima(فاطمه) to Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

464
00:30:38,963 --> 00:30:43,295
So now, Rasool Allah ﷺ has a relationship, family relationship

465
00:30:43,596 --> 00:30:46,161
with the four Khulafa'a رضي الله عنهم.

466
00:30:48,853 --> 00:30:56,073
Two things here to note, number one marriage in those days was very easy, very easy.

467
00:30:57,024 --> 00:30:59,746
Now we have complicated marriage so much

468
00:31:00,561 --> 00:31:03,774
we have placed so much bureaucracy in marriage.

469
00:31:05,361 --> 00:31:07,916
That unfortunately Haram(حرام) became easier than Halal(حلال).

470
00:31:10,217 --> 00:31:13,207
In the time of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, things were very simple.

471
00:31:13,605 --> 00:31:17,162
First of all, the nature of the Sahabah(صحابه), as Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) says:

472
00:31:17,186 --> 00:31:18,537
كانو أقَّلِّ النَاس تكلفا

473
00:31:18,590 --> 00:31:23,212
They were the least superficial among people, they hated complications

474
00:31:24,004 --> 00:31:27,745
and they lived a very simple life, and they loved simplicity.

475
00:31:29,111 --> 00:31:31,838
They were the furthest from complication or sophistication.

476
00:31:32,917 --> 00:31:37,155
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم were simple in their dress, simple in their food

477
00:31:37,564 --> 00:31:43,244
simple in their furniture, simpler in their houses, simple in everything.

478
00:31:44,178 --> 00:31:49,122
And they cherished and they loved that simplicity, it is not like, that's all what they knew

479
00:31:49,215 --> 00:31:50,632
No! Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) says:

480
00:31:50,706 --> 00:31:54,239
I have knowledge about all of these fancy dishes and food.

481
00:31:55,459 --> 00:32:00,113
But this is how I want to live, I want to live simplicity, it's not due to ignorance.

482
00:32:01,443 --> 00:32:03,112
They viewed that as a better way.

483
00:32:03,870 --> 00:32:05,508
So marriage was very simple.

484
00:32:06,225 --> 00:32:10,556
And you can notice that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه is offering his daughter, who would do that today.

485
00:32:12,172 --> 00:32:15,865
Who would go to somebody whom they know is a good person, a righteous person

486
00:32:15,890 --> 00:32:18,971
a brother who is in need of marriage, and then tell them.

487
00:32:19,545 --> 00:32:21,493
I would offer you my daughter who would do that now?

488
00:32:22,880 --> 00:32:26,483
They just think that it's just shame, it's embarrassing, it's not good,

489
00:32:27,362 --> 00:32:31,378
it's lower in your status, but Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) didn't have a problem with that

490
00:32:31,481 --> 00:32:33,877
he went and he offered his daughter to Uthman(عثمان)

491
00:32:33,997 --> 00:32:36,631
he offered her to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

492
00:32:36,783 --> 00:32:38,540
because he wants the best for his daughter.

493
00:32:39,802 --> 00:32:44,013
And in those days because marriage was so simple and easy.

494
00:32:44,986 --> 00:32:47,399
There wasn't anything called an unmarried woman

495
00:32:48,551 --> 00:32:52,149
which is called an Arabic Unoosa(عنوسه), woman who are unmarried

496
00:32:52,254 --> 00:32:56,035
who're deprived from the blessing of marriage.

497
00:32:56,642 --> 00:32:59,903
In those days there was a rule that you take care of every woman in the society

498
00:33:00,984 --> 00:33:02,668
every woman would be taken care of.

499
00:33:03,485 --> 00:33:10,823
So one of the purposes of polygamy was, so that the whole society is taken care of.

500
00:33:11,311 --> 00:33:13,924
Nobody is left out of this important relationship.

501
00:33:14,546 --> 00:33:17,748
Because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has created us in pairs, Azwaaja(أزواج).

502
00:33:19,042 --> 00:33:25,053
And it's part of the nature of the man and a woman to be in such a relationship.

503
00:33:25,886 --> 00:33:29,344
So therefore no one in the society would be left out and deprived of this

504
00:33:29,903 --> 00:33:34,143
and Rasool Allah ﷺ told the ones, who wanted to choose a different path

505
00:33:34,569 --> 00:33:35,635
that this is not my Sunnah(سنة).

506
00:33:36,233 --> 00:33:40,603
The ones, who wanted to practice a life of celibacy and get away from marriage

507
00:33:40,973 --> 00:33:44,912
because they heard that this was the practice of the Christian monks

508
00:33:45,215 --> 00:33:47,831
Rasool Allah ﷺ said this is not my Sunnah(سنة), this is not my way,

509
00:33:49,070 --> 00:33:53,906
my way is the way of marriage and whoever doesn't follow my way, doesn't belong to me.

510
00:33:55,205 --> 00:33:58,689
So marriage in Islam is Ibadah(عبادة), it's form of worship

511
00:33:59,740 --> 00:34:01,652
and we please Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ through it.

512
00:34:03,263 --> 00:34:09,904
So, I would like to urge all the parents to make marriage easy,

513
00:34:10,690 --> 00:34:14,184
so that they can keep their boys and girls away from Haram(حرام).

514
00:34:15,308 --> 00:34:19,301
In the time of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم Halaal(حلال) was easier than Haram(حرام)

515
00:34:20,120 --> 00:34:23,586
Haram(حرام) was very difficult to commit Haram(حرام) was very difficult.

516
00:34:24,668 --> 00:34:26,476
But the path of Halaal(حلال) was very easy.

517
00:34:29,528 --> 00:34:32,754
However, now things, especially in Western societies

518
00:34:33,008 --> 00:34:36,374
every Haram(حرام) is available and it's not only available it's promoted.

519
00:34:38,268 --> 00:34:41,113
Because we are living in times when good is evil and evil is good.

520
00:34:41,608 --> 00:34:48,637
So this is something that the Muslim families need to break these rigid traditions that don't belong to Islam.

521
00:34:49,077 --> 00:34:53,911
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) as a scholar say every Bid'ah(بدعة) replaces a Sunnah(سنة)

522
00:34:55,306 --> 00:34:59,785
everything wrong is only there because it has uprooted something that was right.

523
00:35:01,366 --> 00:35:06,750
Therefore we should go back to the way of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم in making things simple and encouraging Halaal(حلال),

524
00:35:06,822 --> 00:35:07,924
 and Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

525
00:35:07,964 --> 00:35:09,848
من استطاع منكم باه في اليتزوج

526
00:35:10,414 --> 00:35:12,361
Marriage should be done in an early age.

527
00:35:13,657 --> 00:35:17,544
We ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to make it easy on our brothers and sisters, who are seeking marriage

528
00:35:17,839 --> 00:35:20,498
 to make Halal(حلال) an open door for them

529
00:35:20,823 --> 00:35:23,265
and to close the doors of Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) in their faces.

530
00:35:27,038 --> 00:35:29,248
Rasool Allah ﷺ was giving Khutba Al-Jumu'ah(خطبة الجمعه).

531
00:35:31,665 --> 00:35:36,274
When the caravan came in to Madina.

532
00:35:38,061 --> 00:35:45,038
They used to sent out caravans to go to Ash-sham(ألشام) and to Yemen to bring back merchandise.

533
00:35:46,017 --> 00:35:51,636
So these caravans would come back a few times a year, and the caravan would be led by a group of men

534
00:35:51,707 --> 00:35:54,832
and it includes the money of the whole community.

535
00:35:55,834 --> 00:36:00,610
So everybody would invest in that caravan, to go out and they would all wait for it

536
00:36:00,727 --> 00:36:05,084
in anticipation, eager for its return that was their livelihood.

537
00:36:05,603 --> 00:36:08,198
So it was a very, very big event when the caravan arrives

538
00:36:08,231 --> 00:36:10,420
and everybody jumps in there to get the best deal.

539
00:36:11,315 --> 00:36:15,907
It happened that the caravan arrived when Rasool Allah ﷺ was giving Khutba Al-Jumu'ah(خطبة الجمعه).

540
00:36:17,970 --> 00:36:22,375
And the rules of Jumu'ah(جمعه) are still not clear in terms of you're not supposed to move

541
00:36:22,415 --> 00:36:23,939
and you're not supposed to speak

542
00:36:24,923 --> 00:36:26,105
so everyone left the Masjid(مسجد)

543
00:36:28,570 --> 00:36:31,608
and only a few remained with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

544
00:36:33,112 --> 00:36:37,425
It wasn't mandatory yet for them to remain, at least that's how we would assume

545
00:36:38,171 --> 00:36:43,179
we wouldn't imagine that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم would leave when they have an understanding that it's mandatory.

546
00:36:45,271 --> 00:36:49,652
So it must have been before the final rules of Jumu'ah(جمعه) were given, so they left.

547
00:36:51,102 --> 00:36:53,818
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ revealed the Ayah(آية) in Surat-Ul-Jumu'ah(سورة الجمعه).

548
00:36:56,588 --> 00:37:00,802
وَإِذَا رَأَوْا تِجَارَةً أَوْ لَهْوًا انفَضُّوا إِلَيْهَا وَتَرَكُوكَ قَائِمًا

549
00:37:01,176 --> 00:37:05,454
قُلْ مَا عِندَ اللَّهِ خَيْرٌ مِّنَ اللَّهْوِ وَمِنَ التِّجَارَةِ ۚ وَاللَّهُ خَيْرُ الرَّازِقِينَ۝

550
00:37:06,075 --> 00:37:10,244
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says, but when they saw a transaction or diversion

551
00:37:10,401 --> 00:37:14,127
O Muhammad(محمد), they rushed to it, and left you standing

552
00:37:15,240 --> 00:37:20,827
say what is with Allah is better than diversion, and then a transaction

553
00:37:21,092 --> 00:37:22,783
and Allah is the best of providers.

554
00:37:24,334 --> 00:37:28,035
They left, and you were standing in the Masjid(مسجد)

555
00:37:29,196 --> 00:37:33,353
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is saying that what Allah has is better than this business

556
00:37:33,804 --> 00:37:35,862
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is the One, Who gives Rizq(رزق).

557
00:37:36,202 --> 00:37:38,988
You left Salaat-Ul-Jumu'ah(جمعه), to go and meet the caravan

558
00:37:39,243 --> 00:37:41,025
while Rasool Allah ﷺ was giving Kht'bah(خطبه).

559
00:37:41,395 --> 00:37:47,049
Now it says, in the narration of this statement that only 12 remained

560
00:37:47,459 --> 00:37:51,265
and among those 12 were Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar رضي الله عنهما.

561
00:37:52,410 --> 00:37:54,578
So you would find them always on the right side

562
00:37:56,112 --> 00:37:59,053
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar رضي الله عنهما even though both of them were businessmen

563
00:37:59,125 --> 00:38:03,047
and they had a lot of interest to go and meet the caravan, but they stayed behind

564
00:38:03,457 --> 00:38:05,351
until Rasool Allah ﷺ finishes his Khut'bah(خطبة).

565
00:38:05,659 --> 00:38:09,042
So they were not included among the ones in this Ayah(آية).

566
00:38:11,343 --> 00:38:14,309
Rasool Allah ﷺ says, in a Hadith(حديث) in Bukhari(بخاريْ)

567
00:38:14,334 --> 00:38:18,487
من جرَّا ثوبه’ خيالآء لم ننظر الله عليه يوم القيامة

568
00:38:19,593 --> 00:38:29,303
If your Izaar(إزار) is dragging, under the ankle out of pride and showing off,

569
00:38:29,613 --> 00:38:33,111
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will not look at you, on the Day of Judgment.

570
00:38:34,474 --> 00:38:38,980
So the Sunnah(وکع) is to wear the clothes, above the ankle.

571
00:38:39,602 --> 00:38:42,144
Now, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), as I mentioned was very slim.

572
00:38:44,148 --> 00:38:48,661
So when he would tie his Izaar(إزار) around his waist, because of his thinness

573
00:38:49,063 --> 00:38:53,774
his Izaar(إزار) would slip, he was very slim so it wouldn't hold on his waist.

574
00:38:54,411 --> 00:38:56,879
So he told Rasool Allah ﷺ, O Messenger of Allah,

575
00:38:57,324 --> 00:39:03,414
My Izaar(إزار) wouldn't hold to my waist and it would slip down and go under the ankle

576
00:39:03,439 --> 00:39:07,563
and the only way for me to keep it above the ankle is to continue all the time tugging it up.

577
00:39:08,400 --> 00:39:12,068
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him that you are not among the ones

578
00:39:12,092 --> 00:39:14,747
who are doing it out of pride, out of arrogance.

579
00:39:15,540 --> 00:39:20,103
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: You are not included in this Hadith(حديث).

580
00:39:20,734 --> 00:39:23,933
So this is a Shahadah(شهادة) from Rasool Allah ﷺ

581
00:39:24,456 --> 00:39:31,665
that Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is free from arrogance, and we know how great of a sin arrogance is.

582
00:39:32,646 --> 00:39:37,776
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: Whoever has a single grain of arrogance in their hearts will not even smell paradise.

583
00:39:38,550 --> 00:39:41,340
So we ask Allah سبحانه وتعالى to keep us away from this evil sin

584
00:39:41,781 --> 00:39:44,946
which has brought the demise of Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ), Iblees(إبليس).

585
00:39:45,282 --> 00:39:49,846
That's how Iblees(إبليس) lost his very high status among the angels.

586
00:39:50,116 --> 00:39:52,126
It is because of arrogance.

587
00:39:52,277 --> 00:39:52,958
أنا خير منه

588
00:39:52,982 --> 00:39:53,956
I'm better than him!

589
00:39:54,336 --> 00:39:57,242
Why should I make Sujood(سجود) for him, while, I'm better than him?

590
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:03,585
And that's why they say that the worst thing for Iblees(إبليس) is to see you making Sujood(سجود)

591
00:40:04,431 --> 00:40:09,253
because his refusal of Sujood(سجود) is what brought the wrath of Allah on him.

592
00:40:10,319 --> 00:40:13,188
And when he sees the Muslim making Sujood(سجود)

593
00:40:13,212 --> 00:40:16,482
he knows that this is what will bring the Mercy of Allah on that person

594
00:40:16,506 --> 00:40:18,242
so he hates, he dislikes Sujood(سجود).

595
00:40:19,285 --> 00:40:21,727
You anger Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) when you make Sujood(سجود) to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

596
00:40:22,277 --> 00:40:23,219
Because Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) says:

597
00:40:23,473 --> 00:40:27,195
أمرت بسجود فلم أسجد وامر إبن آدم بالسجود فسجد

598
00:40:27,448 --> 00:40:29,814
I was ordered to make Sujood(سجود) and I refused

599
00:40:30,044 --> 00:40:32,884
and the son of Adam(آدم) was ordered to make Sujood(سجود) and he did.

600
00:40:34,912 --> 00:40:35,973
Number four:

601
00:40:37,473 --> 00:40:42,484
During Eid(عيد) Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه went to visit his daughter Ayesha(عائشه).

602
00:40:43,894 --> 00:40:50,143
He comes in and he finds two young girls from the Ansaar(أنْصَار) singing for her

603
00:40:51,640 --> 00:40:54,893
special performance for Ayesha رضي الله عنها.

604
00:40:57,413 --> 00:41:02,638
No instruments were used in this according to this particular narration, they were singing.

605
00:41:03,565 --> 00:41:07,184
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, when he saw that he was very angry and he said:

606
00:41:07,208 --> 00:41:10,594
أبى مضموع الشيطان في بيت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

607
00:41:11,122 --> 00:41:14,682
You're using the flute of the devil in the house of Rasool Allah ﷺ

608
00:41:15,256 --> 00:41:18,608
singing in the house of Muhammad صلوات الله والسلام عليه

609
00:41:18,633 --> 00:41:20,094
he was very upset with his daughter.

610
00:41:20,629 --> 00:41:26,727
But Rasool Allah ﷺ was there and Rasool Allah ﷺ was facing the wall

611
00:41:26,751 --> 00:41:29,001
so he didn't see Ayesha(عائشه) and he didn’t see Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

612
00:41:29,302 --> 00:41:32,356
but he spoke to them without looking back. He said;

613
00:41:33,743 --> 00:41:38,143
يا أبا بكر إنَّا لكل قومٍ عيدا وهذ عيدنا

614
00:41:38,686 --> 00:41:39,593
And this is in Muslim(ألمسلم).

615
00:41:40,077 --> 00:41:40,907
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

616
00:41:40,931 --> 00:41:44,571
O Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), every people have a celebration.

617
00:41:44,976 --> 00:41:48,908
And this is our celebration, Eid, a day of celebration.

618
00:41:50,803 --> 00:41:53,616
Rasool Allah ﷺ approved what Ayesha(عائشه) was doing

619
00:41:54,135 --> 00:41:57,230
and Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

620
00:41:57,531 --> 00:42:02,193
that in situations like these, it is appropriate and fine to celebrate

621
00:42:02,283 --> 00:42:04,203
and Rasool Allah ﷺ says in another Hadith(حديث).

622
00:42:04,410 --> 00:42:07,528
ليعمل المشركون أنَّ في ديننا فصحا

623
00:42:08,251 --> 00:42:10,763
We want the Mushrikeen(مشركين), the disbelievers to know

624
00:42:10,984 --> 00:42:13,847
that there is room for entertainment in our religion.

625
00:42:14,248 --> 00:42:20,249
There is room for one to entertain themselves as long as it's done in a Halal(حلال) fashion.

626
00:42:20,659 --> 00:42:30,900
So, as a human being there is a compartment, in your compartments of needs of entertainment

627
00:42:32,384 --> 00:42:36,807
your soul and your heart and your body needs this.

628
00:42:38,358 --> 00:42:39,876
It is different according to people

629
00:42:39,900 --> 00:42:45,189
some people their compartment of entertainment is larger than others but everybody has a need.

630
00:42:45,934 --> 00:42:49,935
Obviously in Islam, we're encouraged to be serious

631
00:42:50,439 --> 00:42:51,982
because this is a serious religion.

632
00:42:52,744 --> 00:42:53,938
 And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

633
00:42:53,986 --> 00:42:55,675
يَا يَحْيَىٰ خُذِ الْكِتَابَ بِقُوَّةٍ ۖ

634
00:42:55,699 --> 00:42:58,215
Oh Yahya(يحي), hold the book with strength and power

635
00:42:59,251 --> 00:43:01,582
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says to Banni Israel(بني اسرائيل):

636
00:43:01,969 --> 00:43:03,822
خُذُوا مَا آتَيْنَاكُمْ بِقُوَّةٍ

637
00:43:04,100 --> 00:43:07,263
Take what We have given you, the commands We have given you with strength.

638
00:43:07,783 --> 00:43:14,423
So the religion is serious, but then there is on the side, time for one to entertain their souls.

639
00:43:14,907 --> 00:43:19,592
But we shouldn't turn the whole religion into entertainment and fun

640
00:43:19,617 --> 00:43:22,462
because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says about the disbelievers.

641
00:43:23,318 --> 00:43:25,313
اتَّخَذُوا دِينَهُمْ لَعِبًا وَلَهْوًا

642
00:43:25,552 --> 00:43:28,123
They have taken the religion to be an entertainment and fun

643
00:43:29,729 --> 00:43:35,089
And in the Masjid(مسجد) I used to be the Imam(اِمَام) in the U.S.

644
00:43:35,562 --> 00:43:41,726
We used to have some church groups, visit us, and they would come and see the Salah(صلاة)

645
00:43:43,144 --> 00:43:45,939
they would be impressed with the Salah(صلاة), they would like it they would see the Khut'ba(خطبه)

646
00:43:45,979 --> 00:43:49,196
they would see the Ibadah(عبادة) of the Muslims in Masjid(مسجد)

647
00:43:49,607 --> 00:43:56,907
but quite often, they would ask the question, you don't have any singing in your Mosques.?

648
00:43:57,802 --> 00:44:01,869
You don't have any group to sing and perform for you in the mosque?

649
00:44:02,146 --> 00:44:04,385
We would say: No! This is our Ibadah(عبادة) this is how it is.

650
00:44:04,873 --> 00:44:07,256
They would view it as very bland and plain.

651
00:44:08,312 --> 00:44:13,450
That is because they got used to singing and entertainment in the church

652
00:44:13,490 --> 00:44:20,313
 and I had a professor in social sciences, who was an atheist.

653
00:44:20,997 --> 00:44:24,595
He didn't believe in God, but he said: I still like to go to the church,

654
00:44:24,970 --> 00:44:26,180
because I love the songs.

655
00:44:29,371 --> 00:44:31,907
But Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) even though there's no singing in the Masjid(مسجد)

656
00:44:31,932 --> 00:44:37,078
and there's no entertainment in the sense of the modern definition of entertainment

657
00:44:38,346 --> 00:44:41,977
but Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ puts a certain Sakinah(سكينه) in the heart because being in the masjid(مسجد).

658
00:44:42,555 --> 00:44:45,994
When you hear the Qur'an, the lining up in the Salah(صلاة)

659
00:44:46,483 --> 00:44:50,121
the movement in cohesion with everybody else.

660
00:44:51,051 --> 00:44:52,766
The whole sight of Salah(صلاة) is impressive

661
00:44:53,270 --> 00:44:58,712
and when you see the sight of 2 million people in Salah At-Taraweeh(ألصلاة التراويح) in Al-Haram(ألحرم),

662
00:44:59,212 --> 00:45:01,830
 making Sujood(سجود) together, making Rukooh(ركوع) together

663
00:45:02,224 --> 00:45:06,048
listening to the recitation of Qur'an, it's a very powerful scene.

664
00:45:06,998 --> 00:45:09,593
When you look at Hajj(حَجْ), there's no singing going on, in Hajj(حَجْ)

665
00:45:09,966 --> 00:45:11,230
but it's a powerful image.

666
00:45:12,599 --> 00:45:15,368
So Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), a Muslim who experiences this.

667
00:45:16,802 --> 00:45:20,606
just think about - how the deprived the person is,

668
00:45:20,853 --> 00:45:22,649
if they don't have Salah(صلاة) in their lives.

669
00:45:23,595 --> 00:45:25,671
Could you imagine living without making Sujood(سجود)

670
00:45:26,191 --> 00:45:28,430
can you imagine living without Salaat-Ul-Jama'ah(صلاةالجماعة)

671
00:45:29,371 --> 00:45:32,312
can you imagine living without having the concept of Ramadan(رمضان)

672
00:45:32,931 --> 00:45:37,545
no fasting, no Taraweeh(تراويح), no breaking your fast, that happiness and pleasure

673
00:45:37,811 --> 00:45:40,549
that comes with eating the first dates, when you're hungry.

674
00:45:41,061 --> 00:45:43,131
Can you imagine how deprive the person would be

675
00:45:43,156 --> 00:45:46,439
when they don't have the concept of Hajj(حَجْ), they don't know what Hajj(حَجْ) is

676
00:45:46,591 --> 00:45:48,221
they never seen it, they never experienced it

677
00:45:49,826 --> 00:45:51,997
without having the celebration of Eid(عيد).

678
00:45:52,479 --> 00:45:57,265
So even though there's no singing, and entertainment in Islam, but it is so fulfilling.

679
00:45:57,746 --> 00:46:01,510
It makes your life, full, with joy and happiness.

680
00:46:01,844 --> 00:46:04,085
Ibn Taymiyyah(إبن تيمية) when they, put him in jail

681
00:46:04,109 --> 00:46:06,381
and then they threatened him to do this and that. He said:

682
00:46:06,405 --> 00:46:09,551
What can my enemy do with me.? My Jannah(جنة) is in my heart

683
00:46:10,102 --> 00:46:11,920
my Paradise is in my heart.

684
00:46:12,575 --> 00:46:16,304
 If they put me in jail I will use that time to make Zikr(زكر) of Allah.

685
00:46:16,740 --> 00:46:18,667
And if they kill me, I am a Shaheed(شهيد).

686
00:46:18,778 --> 00:46:19,578
So what can they do.

687
00:46:20,871 --> 00:46:23,226
So the Mo'min(مؤمن) is carrying the Jannah(جنة)

688
00:46:23,250 --> 00:46:26,491
the pleasure, the tranquility with them in their hearts.

689
00:46:29,183 --> 00:46:31,550
For those of you, who have experienced in Masjid-Al-Nabwi(مسجد ألنبوي).

690
00:46:32,864 --> 00:46:36,147
I mean, imagine how the deprived the person is, if they never have a chance

691
00:46:36,171 --> 00:46:38,568
to sit inside Ar-Raodha(ألروضه), which is part of Jannah(جنة).

692
00:46:40,088 --> 00:46:43,423
So Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has blessed us and we shouldn't take this for granted and we should say;

693
00:46:43,463 --> 00:46:44,854
 ألحمدلله رب العلمين

694
00:46:45,284 --> 00:46:48,075
We don't have any musical instruments going on in the Masjid(مسجد)

695
00:46:48,361 --> 00:46:53,283
but it's more fulfilling than the best musical concert in the world.

696
00:46:54,879 --> 00:46:57,086
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has blessed us and we should say Alhamdolillah(ألحمدلله).

697
00:46:59,067 --> 00:47:05,070
But again, we have to fulfill that deep need inside for entertainment.

698
00:47:05,582 --> 00:47:09,212
And that's why, for example, that's one of the purposes of marriage.

699
00:47:10,841 --> 00:47:12,274
وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَكُم مَّوَدَّةً وَرَحْمَةً ۚ

700
00:47:12,298 --> 00:47:16,301
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has made between the man and woman, mercy, and compassion

701
00:47:17,868 --> 00:47:22,353
and there are many forms of entertainment that serve a dual purpose.

702
00:47:24,997 --> 00:47:30,566
Like sports, not only is this a form of entertainment for you but it's also preparation.

703
00:47:33,008 --> 00:47:36,940
So we ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to give us the correct understanding in His religion

704
00:47:36,988 --> 00:47:38,928
because both extremes are very dangerous.

705
00:47:41,987 --> 00:47:45,765
We also noticed that this wasn't the habit

706
00:47:46,543 --> 00:47:50,642
Otherwise Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would not say what he said.

707
00:47:51,397 --> 00:47:54,778
So it wasn't the habit that they always have singing going on

708
00:47:55,689 --> 00:47:57,109
it was a once in a while thing.

709
00:47:58,457 --> 00:48:04,615
And according to the majority of the scholars all instruments are not allowed, with the exception of the tambourine.

710
00:48:05,509 --> 00:48:09,956
This situation Ayesha رضي الله عنها  had two young girls from an Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار), singing for her.

711
00:48:11,035 --> 00:48:13,475
The generosity of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

712
00:48:13,752 --> 00:48:16,257
In Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(ألمسلم), you know about Ahlus Suffah(أهل الصفه)

713
00:48:16,282 --> 00:48:23,638
they were named Ahlus Suffah(أهل الصفه) these were the poor Sahabah(صحابه), mostly Muhajireen(مهاجرين)

714
00:48:24,171 --> 00:48:27,843
from Makkah or from other places, who didn't have houses in Madina.

715
00:48:28,386 --> 00:48:31,252
So they ended up staying in a corner, in the Masjid(مسجد).

716
00:48:32,795 --> 00:48:35,206
They are very poor, they couldn't afford buying a house

717
00:48:35,413 --> 00:48:39,249
so Rasool Allah ﷺ allowed them to stay in a certain corner in the Masjid(مسجد)

718
00:48:40,214 --> 00:48:43,697
those were their living quarters in the Masjid(مسجد) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

719
00:48:44,184 --> 00:48:45,430
and it wasn't only the poor

720
00:48:45,455 --> 00:48:48,394
but sometimes also the young among the Sahabah(صحابه) would go and join them.

721
00:48:48,871 --> 00:48:50,827
So Abdullah Ibn Umar رضي الله عنه said;

722
00:48:51,261 --> 00:48:54,396
I spent two years in Masjid(مسجد) before I got married.

723
00:48:55,086 --> 00:48:58,672
He would stay in Masjid(مسجد) full time in order to be close to Rasool Allah ﷺ

724
00:48:58,696 --> 00:49:02,186
because that's where Rasool Allah ﷺ would conduct his lesson.

725
00:49:03,184 --> 00:49:03,619
He said:

726
00:49:03,659 --> 00:49:04,357
وانا اللعازب,

727
00:49:04,397 --> 00:49:07,933
when I was a bachelor I spent two years in the Masjid(مسجد) not because he was poor,

728
00:49:08,173 --> 00:49:11,735
 his father Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه was quite well off.

729
00:49:12,105 --> 00:49:15,990
So he would spend time in the Masjid(مسجد) to be close to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

730
00:49:18,315 --> 00:49:23,751
Rasool Allah ﷺ said to the Sahabah(صحابه) in that particular night,

731
00:49:24,108 --> 00:49:28,010
 if you have food for two take a third person with you

732
00:49:28,600 --> 00:49:31,922
if you had food for three, take a fourth person

733
00:49:32,380 --> 00:49:35,802
if you had food for four, take a fifth person.

734
00:49:37,385 --> 00:49:40,857
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to provide food for Ahlus-Suffah(أهل الصفة) that night

735
00:49:41,736 --> 00:49:46,184
and Rasool Allah ﷺ told the Sahabah(صحابه), the food for two is enough for three

736
00:49:46,602 --> 00:49:48,989
and the food of three is enough for four

737
00:49:49,100 --> 00:49:52,798
and the food the four is enough for five, if Allah puts Barakah(بركة) in it.

738
00:49:55,037 --> 00:49:59,816
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he took three, took them to his house

739
00:50:00,164 --> 00:50:05,184
and entrusted them to Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) his son, but then Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) left

740
00:50:05,465 --> 00:50:08,594
and he went to join Rasool Allah ﷺ, and he had dinner with Rasool Ullah.

741
00:50:11,005 --> 00:50:12,704
An- Nawawi(ألنووي) comments on this and says

742
00:50:12,783 --> 00:50:15,400
that this shows that Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

743
00:50:15,924 --> 00:50:20,253
would put the importance of spending his time with Rasool Allah ﷺ

744
00:50:20,277 --> 00:50:24,676
above his family, above his children, above his guests, and above everything.

745
00:50:25,150 --> 00:50:27,304
So he took the guest to his house and then he went

746
00:50:27,707 --> 00:50:31,035
rather than having dinner with his guests, he went to have it with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

747
00:50:31,289 --> 00:50:35,342
Because Rasool Ullah took 10 with him, he took 10 from among Ahlus-Suffah(أهل الصفة)

748
00:50:36,090 --> 00:50:37,376
and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) took three.

749
00:50:39,060 --> 00:50:41,780
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه told his family to feed them

750
00:50:42,699 --> 00:50:44,684
and Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) was there at home.

751
00:50:46,798 --> 00:50:51,425
He ended up spending a lot of time with Rasool Allah ﷺ and he came back home, very late.

752
00:50:52,606 --> 00:50:59,785
The wife of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: How come you were late and you didn't feed your guests?

753
00:51:00,335 --> 00:51:02,380
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said: You didn't feed them yet!

754
00:51:02,900 --> 00:51:04,310
She said: No! They refused.

755
00:51:05,181 --> 00:51:07,273
Abdur Rahman Bin Abi Bakr(عبدالرحمن إبن أبي بكر), he said:

756
00:51:07,297 --> 00:51:09,614
When I heard that, I ran away to hide

757
00:51:09,938 --> 00:51:11,935
because I know that my father would be very upset.

758
00:51:12,306 --> 00:51:17,257
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) was not a child at that time he was, he was very old, he's already fought in battles,

759
00:51:17,916 --> 00:51:19,797
 but he still was afraid of his father.

760
00:51:20,972 --> 00:51:24,564
So he said: I went in hiding, and my father called me Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن)

761
00:51:24,588 --> 00:51:27,985
the first time, I didn't respond, second time Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن), didn't respond

762
00:51:28,325 --> 00:51:32,414
third time he said: Ya Ghanfar(يا غنفر), Ghanfar(غنفر) is a small fly, blue fly

763
00:51:32,793 --> 00:51:36,228
Ya Ghanfar(يا غنفر)! I knew that he is serious, I responded!

764
00:51:37,474 --> 00:51:39,207
He said: Why didn't you feed them?

765
00:51:40,295 --> 00:51:42,515
So I took my father to them and I said;

766
00:51:42,695 --> 00:51:45,292
Didn't I tell you to eat and you refused and that was true

767
00:51:45,454 --> 00:51:49,993
Abdur Rahman Ibn Abi Bakr(عبدالرحمن إبن أبي بكر) insisted on them to eat

768
00:51:50,232 --> 00:51:52,783
but they said: We are not going to eat this, they said: In the Name of Allah

769
00:51:52,808 --> 00:51:55,595
we're not going to eat until Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) comes back.

770
00:51:56,341 --> 00:51:57,721
He said: Go ahead and eat this.

771
00:51:57,761 --> 00:51:59,226
They said: No! We won't, we're gonna wait for him.

772
00:51:59,903 --> 00:52:03,704
So he told his father, listen! I tried, but they are the ones, who refused.

773
00:52:04,716 --> 00:52:06,473
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said: Why didn't you eat?

774
00:52:06,593 --> 00:52:08,612
And he was upset with the guests

775
00:52:08,637 --> 00:52:10,513
I mean, why did you have to wait for all of this time.

776
00:52:11,619 --> 00:52:16,369
And nobody told me and I brought you here to host you.

777
00:52:17,397 --> 00:52:19,934
Why did you end up spending all these hours waiting for me?

778
00:52:20,696 --> 00:52:22,946
So I'm not going to eat you go ahead and eat, they said;

779
00:52:22,970 --> 00:52:25,522
In the name of Allah, we're not going to eat until you eat with us.

780
00:52:26,573 --> 00:52:30,203
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said, that's from Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ), and he sat down

781
00:52:30,551 --> 00:52:31,914
what he meant by that is from Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ),

782
00:52:31,938 --> 00:52:34,005
the oath that he made that he's not going to eat with them

783
00:52:34,089 --> 00:52:36,312
and when he saw that they insisted on him eating

784
00:52:36,337 --> 00:52:38,536
and they made an oath in the name of Allah, that he should eat.

785
00:52:38,900 --> 00:52:42,424
He broke his oath, and that is a known in Islam that

786
00:52:42,686 --> 00:52:48,522
if you make an oath in something and then something better comes in terms of goodness

787
00:52:48,869 --> 00:52:51,396
then you do, what is good you make Takfeer(تكفير),

788
00:52:51,978 --> 00:52:54,587
you pay for the oath that you made.

789
00:52:56,369 --> 00:52:59,415
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه sat with them to eat.

790
00:53:01,146 --> 00:53:01,827
He said;

791
00:53:02,190 --> 00:53:04,288
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) is saying is the one who's narrating this Hadith(حديث)

792
00:53:04,328 --> 00:53:05,487
it's in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم).

793
00:53:06,249 --> 00:53:10,618
He said: Whenever we would take a mouthful, more food would appear.

794
00:53:12,052 --> 00:53:17,817
We keep on taking food more food appears, We eat more food, He said:

795
00:53:17,841 --> 00:53:23,049
The food was growing in the pot, they all were full.

796
00:53:23,655 --> 00:53:26,779
I took the plate back to my wife and said: Look at it.

797
00:53:28,354 --> 00:53:32,673
And she was amazed to see that the plate came with more food on it

798
00:53:32,912 --> 00:53:34,001
than when she sent it.

799
00:53:35,622 --> 00:53:39,251
And then Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه took it to the house of Rasool Allah ﷺ

800
00:53:39,419 --> 00:53:41,607
and some of the other Ahlus-Suffah(أهل الصفة) ate from it

801
00:53:42,041 --> 00:53:43,447
and again it was increasing.

802
00:53:44,013 --> 00:53:46,865
It was a Karmah(كرامة) that happened to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

803
00:53:46,889 --> 00:53:48,962
It is one of the Karamaat(كرامات) of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

804
00:53:49,107 --> 00:53:52,968
A Mo'ijiza(معجزة) happens to Nabi(نَبِي) a Karmah(كرامة) happens to a Wali(ولي)

805
00:53:53,339 --> 00:53:54,574
you have the Mo'jizaat(معجزات)

806
00:53:54,598 --> 00:53:57,080
and these only happened to Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

807
00:53:57,373 --> 00:54:00,610
and then the Karamaat(كرامات) happened to the friends of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

808
00:54:00,735 --> 00:54:04,682
So this was a Karmah(كرامة) that occurred to Sayidina(سيدنا) Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

809
00:54:06,208 --> 00:54:08,469
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was very generous

810
00:54:09,216 --> 00:54:13,069
and his generosity was very well known, and he would be the one

811
00:54:13,094 --> 00:54:16,599
who would always take care of the bill, whenever he's with Rasool Allah ﷺ

812
00:54:17,611 --> 00:54:18,491
he is the one, who would pay.

813
00:54:19,957 --> 00:54:22,899
when Rasool Allah ﷺ was in the early days of Da'wah(دعوة) in Makkah

814
00:54:24,732 --> 00:54:29,042
Abu Dhar Al-Ghaffari رضي الله عنه came into Makkah to inquire about Muhammadﷺ.

815
00:54:29,075 --> 00:54:31,269
He heard about this man, who was claiming to be a Nabi(نَبِي)

816
00:54:31,709 --> 00:54:32,979
so he wants to know more about him.

817
00:54:33,003 --> 00:54:34,991
Abu Dhar Al-Ghaffari(أبوذرألغفاري) was searching for the truth.

818
00:54:36,853 --> 00:54:41,263
He came into Makkah but because the Da'wah(دعوة) was secret in Makkah.

819
00:54:41,659 --> 00:54:44,525
And in those days it was against the law to preach, Islam

820
00:54:44,549 --> 00:54:46,631
it was against the law to practice Islam

821
00:54:46,917 --> 00:54:49,718
it was against the law to even meet with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

822
00:54:50,402 --> 00:54:53,396
So Abu Dhar Al-Ghaffari(أبوذرألغفاري) ended up spending an entire month in Makkah

823
00:54:53,421 --> 00:54:56,115
and he is unable to get access to Muhammadﷺ.

824
00:54:57,752 --> 00:55:01,203
Later on, he ended up meeting Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

825
00:55:01,918 --> 00:55:04,744
Rasool Ullah asked him how did you survive for an entire month.

826
00:55:05,428 --> 00:55:09,210
He said: I survived on nothing but the water of Zam-Zam(زمزم)

827
00:55:11,613 --> 00:55:13,273
حتى تكثرت أكن بتني

828
00:55:13,535 --> 00:55:15,824
Until the flesh on my stomach was folding.

829
00:55:16,133 --> 00:55:21,874
You know, with the Bedouins, they were very fit, flat tummies, no fat.

830
00:55:22,722 --> 00:55:24,125
Abu Dhar Al-Ghaffari(أبوذرألغفاري) said:

831
00:55:24,512 --> 00:55:28,159
Not only was the Water of sons Zam-Zam(زمزم) satisfactory for me

832
00:55:28,216 --> 00:55:33,238
but I ended up gaining weight, flesh started to fold on my stomach now.

833
00:55:33,484 --> 00:55:35,659
Now, flesh folding on stomach is usual for everyone today

834
00:55:36,062 --> 00:55:39,947
I mean, it's not a big deal. Everyone has their skin folding on the stomach

835
00:55:40,092 --> 00:55:43,849
but those days it was an achievement that flesh was folding on your stomach

836
00:55:43,873 --> 00:55:46,391
you gained a lot of weight, they were very fit.

837
00:55:48,840 --> 00:55:49,815
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

838
00:55:49,950 --> 00:55:50,886
إنها طعامٌ يطعم

839
00:55:51,001 --> 00:55:53,501
Yes it is food, if you wanted it to be so, and in another narration.

840
00:55:53,794 --> 00:55:54,498
,وَشِفاعُ ثمر

841
00:55:55,410 --> 00:55:58,301
And it's healing, if you want it to be so, depending on your Niyyah(نية).

842
00:56:00,475 --> 00:56:04,530
If you drink it for Dua(دُعَا), Allah will fulfill your Dua(دُعَا)

843
00:56:04,609 --> 00:56:08,229
if you drink it as medicine, it's medicine, if you drink it as food, it's food.

844
00:56:08,292 --> 00:56:11,544
As long as you have the intention of a Mo'min(مؤمن), a believer.

845
00:56:13,923 --> 00:56:16,561
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Bakr(ابوبكر): Go and feed him!

846
00:56:17,158 --> 00:56:19,169
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه took him to his house

847
00:56:19,193 --> 00:56:23,268
and gave him some raisins from At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف), a special treat.

848
00:56:24,355 --> 00:56:31,231
So it was Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) who would always be on the side of Rasool Allah ﷺ, to take care of these expenses.

849
00:56:33,281 --> 00:56:35,099
It was a friendship of sacrifice.

850
00:56:37,471 --> 00:56:41,996
one day in a battle, the Muslims were going on a Ghazwa(غزوة).

851
00:56:43,483 --> 00:56:46,011
Ayesha رضي الله عنها, she lost her necklace.

852
00:56:47,532 --> 00:56:49,694
So she went around looking for her necklace

853
00:56:50,712 --> 00:56:52,990
and it was time for the army to leave.

854
00:56:53,950 --> 00:56:59,950
As she couldn't find her necklace looking around, right, left, she couldn't find out.

855
00:57:00,626 --> 00:57:02,754
And Rasool Allah ﷺ is waiting for her patiently

856
00:57:04,530 --> 00:57:07,741
and his young wife is going around trying to find her necklace she couldn't find it.

857
00:57:10,043 --> 00:57:13,223
But it was getting very late, nightfall

858
00:57:14,679 --> 00:57:17,162
and the people ended up staying there.

859
00:57:18,160 --> 00:57:22,367
Now everybody knew the reason why Rasool Allah ﷺ ended up camping in that place.

860
00:57:22,657 --> 00:57:26,232
They knew it was because Ayesha رضي الله عنها has lost her necklace.

861
00:57:26,946 --> 00:57:29,731
So they went to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and said: Look at what your daughter has done to us

862
00:57:30,697 --> 00:57:35,090
she made us spend the night in a place where there's no water and we have no water.

863
00:57:36,010 --> 00:57:39,605
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he went to Ayesha(عائشه).

864
00:57:40,321 --> 00:57:44,133
So Ayesha(عائشه) says: I was sitting and Rasool Allah ﷺ was sleeping

865
00:57:44,385 --> 00:57:46,198
and his head was on my thigh.

866
00:57:47,262 --> 00:57:49,288
And Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was saying:

867
00:57:49,348 --> 00:57:53,151
This is what you did to us, and he said he was poking me in my waist.

868
00:57:53,556 --> 00:57:56,198
He was very upset and poking me in my waist and saying:

869
00:57:56,238 --> 00:57:59,877
You made us stay in a place where there's no water and we have no water with us.

870
00:58:00,140 --> 00:58:02,696
Ayesha رضي الله عنها says the only reason I wasn't moving

871
00:58:02,825 --> 00:58:05,000
is because Rasool Allah ﷺ was sleeping on my lap

872
00:58:05,357 --> 00:58:08,309
and my father was poking me in my waist.

873
00:58:10,173 --> 00:58:12,029
She said: We ended up spending the night there.

874
00:58:12,846 --> 00:58:17,840
Next day in the morning we had to leave, I didn't find my necklace, nothing to do so.

875
00:58:18,305 --> 00:58:22,535
She said: I went on my camel and as soon as my camel stood up the necklace was under it.

876
00:58:24,902 --> 00:58:29,248
Now, the people who went to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to complain that it was because of Ayesha(عائشه).

877
00:58:30,064 --> 00:58:30,883
But look at what happened,

878
00:58:31,080 --> 00:58:34,940
because they went to sleep in a place, where there's no water and they had no water with them

879
00:58:34,964 --> 00:58:36,304
and they had to wake up in the morning

880
00:58:36,328 --> 00:58:38,034
and make Wudhoo(وضؤ) and some had to make Ghussl(غسل).

881
00:58:38,948 --> 00:58:41,552
That is when the revelation of Tayammum(تيمم) came down.

882
00:58:42,838 --> 00:58:45,001
That was when the revelation of Tayammum(تيمم) came down.

883
00:58:46,123 --> 00:58:50,208
So the Sahabah(صحابه), came back to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه and said;

884
00:58:50,791 --> 00:58:52,749
This is the Barakah(بركة) of your household.

885
00:58:53,706 --> 00:58:55,131
This is the Barakah(بركة) of your household.

886
00:58:55,195 --> 00:58:59,128
This Ayah(آية) of Tayammum(تيمم) came down, because your daughter lost her necklace,

887
00:58:59,255 --> 00:59:03,161
it is from the Barakaat(بركات) of the household of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

888
00:59:03,391 --> 00:59:04,183
 its a blessing.

889
00:59:06,852 --> 00:59:11,366
One can notice here how Rasool Allah ﷺ would treat his family.

890
00:59:13,042 --> 00:59:16,332
With his wives and servants, and children

891
00:59:16,914 --> 00:59:19,330
Rasool Allah ﷺ was very very accommodating

892
00:59:20,680 --> 00:59:23,567
and Anas Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه says:

893
00:59:24,042 --> 00:59:27,225
I have served Rasool Allah ﷺ for my entire life

894
00:59:27,706 --> 00:59:33,570
I never remember a day when he beat me or chastised me

895
00:59:34,137 --> 00:59:37,580
or reprimands me for anything, for my entire life.

896
00:59:38,967 --> 00:59:40,709
Because he was a servant of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

897
00:59:42,361 --> 00:59:43,947
When Rasool Allah ﷺ came to Madina

898
00:59:43,971 --> 00:59:46,580
the mother of Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said:

899
00:59:46,967 --> 00:59:49,900
I want to be of his assistance to you.

900
00:59:50,059 --> 00:59:52,821
So here is my son, take him as a servant.

901
00:59:53,748 --> 00:59:57,166
Allah Ho Akbar(الله أكبر), she came and gave up her son to Rasool Allah ﷺ to serve him.

902
00:59:58,717 --> 01:00:00,632
And that was the best thing she did for her son.

903
01:00:01,543 --> 01:00:04,530
For Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) to be brought up in the household of Rasool Allah ﷺ

904
01:00:04,578 --> 01:00:08,568
and absorb all of that knowledge and to become one of the narrators of the Ahadith(احاديث)

905
01:00:08,592 --> 01:00:10,737
the greatest narratives of the Ahadith(احاديث) among the top seven.

906
01:00:11,139 --> 01:00:15,199
It was because of this decision of his mother, to send them into that line of work

907
01:00:16,383 --> 01:00:19,789
which was service of Rasool Allah ﷺ to be his servant.

908
01:00:21,372 --> 01:00:24,771
Mothers and fathers need to influence their children in the right way.

909
01:00:25,330 --> 01:00:29,450
She could have sent her son to be a great businessman or to be a great farmer

910
01:00:29,705 --> 01:00:32,211
but she made a very good decision, very wise decision.

911
01:00:32,840 --> 01:00:38,251
She chose what was more pleasing to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and it paid back, immensely.

912
01:00:39,130 --> 01:00:43,056
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has blessed her son, Anas Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه

913
01:00:43,428 --> 01:00:45,306
one of the greatest of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار).

914
01:00:46,373 --> 01:00:49,857
So, don't be so concerned about the Rizq(رزق) of your children

915
01:00:49,881 --> 01:00:53,399
because it's not you who's giving them Rizq(رزق), it's Allah, who is giving them rizq(رزق).

916
01:00:56,174 --> 01:00:57,681
In fact you're benefiting from that rizq(رزق)

917
01:00:57,705 --> 01:01:00,090
because whenever you have a child who was born

918
01:01:00,618 --> 01:01:04,372
the Rizq(رزق) comes with them and you end up consuming some of that

919
01:01:04,396 --> 01:01:05,854
because you're the one who's raising them up.

920
01:01:07,571 --> 01:01:09,537
Every child comes with their own Rizq(رزق).

921
01:01:09,994 --> 01:01:12,878
You did not provide for yourself, how could you provide for your children?

922
01:01:13,429 --> 01:01:17,791
You are not the one, who's making your Rizq(رزق) is coming to you from Allah.

923
01:01:18,069 --> 01:01:20,479
So if you can't do it for yourself how can you do it for your children

924
01:01:20,795 --> 01:01:23,923
therefore care for what's most important, that you save them from Hellfire.

925
01:01:25,169 --> 01:01:28,229
قُوا أَنْفُسَكُمْ وَأَهْلِيكُمْ نَارًا وَقُودُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجَارَةُ

926
01:01:28,390 --> 01:01:31,062
Save yourselves and your families from hellfire.

927
01:01:31,301 --> 01:01:33,419
That's the responsibility of the head of the household

928
01:01:33,814 --> 01:01:36,959
save yourself and your family from Jahannum(جهنم).

929
01:01:39,142 --> 01:01:41,532
When Hadift-Al-Ifq(حادفة ألعفق) happened.

930
01:01:42,943 --> 01:01:48,435
When the rumor was going around about Ayesha رضي الله عنها and they accused her.

931
01:01:49,799 --> 01:01:52,664
One of the poor relatives of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

932
01:01:54,379 --> 01:01:59,428
who was sponsored financially by Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) got involved in this rumor.

933
01:01:59,854 --> 01:02:01,617
I mean, he spoke against Ayesha رضي الله عنها.

934
01:02:02,973 --> 01:02:05,386
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was upset

935
01:02:06,226 --> 01:02:08,163
he's talking about my daughter, negatively.

936
01:02:08,988 --> 01:02:11,710
So he said: I'm not gonna spend any money on him, anymore.

937
01:02:11,792 --> 01:02:17,926
See Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would take care of the entire expenses of some families

938
01:02:19,425 --> 01:02:21,849
and the family of Mustakh(مسطح), was one of them

939
01:02:23,228 --> 01:02:26,386
but because he got involved in this rumor against Ayesha رضي الله عنها

940
01:02:26,410 --> 01:02:28,792
he said: I'm not gonna support him anymore.

941
01:02:28,976 --> 01:02:31,545
The following Ayah(آية) was revealed, talking about Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

942
01:02:31,797 --> 01:02:35,165
and other people who are in the same situation as Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

943
01:02:36,126 --> 01:02:42,201
وَلَا يَأْتَلِ أُولُو الْفَضْلِ مِنكُمْ وَالسَّعَةِ أَن يُؤْتُوا أُولِي الْقُرْبَىٰ وَالْمَسَاكِينَ وَالْمُهَاجِرِينَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ۖ

944
01:02:42,225 --> 01:02:46,265
وَلْيَعْفُوا وَلْيَصْفَحُوا ۗ أَلَا تُحِبُّونَ أَن يَغْفِرَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ ۗ وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ۝

945
01:02:46,527 --> 01:02:52,476
And let not those of virtue among you, and wealth, swear not to give aid to their relatives

946
01:02:52,516 --> 01:02:54,914
 and the needy and the immigrants for the cause of Allah

947
01:02:55,504 --> 01:02:57,588
and let them pardon and overlook.

948
01:02:58,104 --> 01:03:00,826
Would you not like that Allah should forgive you.

949
01:03:01,073 --> 01:03:02,436
And Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.

950
01:03:03,315 --> 01:03:07,317
So Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: And let not those among you of virtue.

951
01:03:07,758 --> 01:03:10,963
So, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is saying that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is a man of virtue

952
01:03:12,686 --> 01:03:16,520
Allah is saying: Don't stop spending on them, don't you want Allah to forgive you.

953
01:03:16,774 --> 01:03:19,710
As soon as Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) heard the Ayah(آية), he said: Yes! I want Allah to forgive me.

954
01:03:20,112 --> 01:03:22,755
And from then on, he started taking care of Mustakh(مسطح) again.

955
01:03:24,096 --> 01:03:27,201
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه continued making doing business

956
01:03:27,226 --> 01:03:29,665
when he was in Madina, he traveled to Syria, Ash-Sham(ألشام)

957
01:03:30,099 --> 01:03:33,078
so he continued doing that to make a living.

958
01:03:33,574 --> 01:03:35,786
Even though he wanted to be close to Rasool Allah ﷺ

959
01:03:35,810 --> 01:03:40,269
but he had to travel to make a living, seeking Rizq(رزق)

960
01:03:41,219 --> 01:03:46,871
he didn't stop, even though he became very busy in his life in Madina.

961
01:03:47,618 --> 01:03:52,812
And with Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه every moment that he would spend in his business, is rewardable

962
01:03:53,099 --> 01:03:56,189
because his money would end up being spent in the sake of Islam.

963
01:03:57,084 --> 01:03:58,718
So really his business was Ibadah(عبادة)

964
01:03:59,426 --> 01:04:03,107
because his wealth was for the service of Rasool Allah ﷺ and the religion.

965
01:04:03,494 --> 01:04:05,782
So it is exactly like he's doing any other Ibadah(عبادة).

966
01:04:08,208 --> 01:04:13,337
We can see that from the narration that I will mention to you now.

967
01:04:14,341 --> 01:04:20,697
That Rasool Allah ﷺ was very grateful to his friendship with Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

968
01:04:21,754 --> 01:04:28,134
Rabia Al-Aslami(ربيعة ألأسلمي), he said that Rasool Allah ﷺ gave me a piece of land

969
01:04:29,607 --> 01:04:33,062
and he gave Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه a piece of land, next to mine.

970
01:04:34,636 --> 01:04:40,142
And then Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) came between me and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and we had a dispute on a palm tree.

971
01:04:41,453 --> 01:04:44,883
I claimed it to be in my land and he claimed it to be in his land.

972
01:04:45,692 --> 01:04:47,050
So we had an argument.

973
01:04:48,653 --> 01:04:52,613
He then said, something to me that made me upset

974
01:04:52,900 --> 01:04:55,550
he said the harsh word that made me upset.

975
01:04:56,788 --> 01:04:59,698
But then he immediately regretted that. And he said;

976
01:05:00,835 --> 01:05:06,477
O Rabiah(ربيعة) reply back to me, so that we can get even.

977
01:05:08,575 --> 01:05:10,047
Look at the nature of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق)

978
01:05:10,071 --> 01:05:13,921
even though he got upset and he mentioned something harsh to Rabiah(ربيعة)

979
01:05:14,292 --> 01:05:17,112
but he immediately came back and he said: No!

980
01:05:17,944 --> 01:05:20,571
I want you, to respond back to me so that we can be even.

981
01:05:21,653 --> 01:05:25,118
Because Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) doesn't have hard feelings against anyone.

982
01:05:26,326 --> 01:05:28,656
So he told him: Reply back to me.

983
01:05:29,942 --> 01:05:31,394
Rabiah(ربيعة) said: I won't!

984
01:05:32,246 --> 01:05:35,538
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: You would reply back to me

985
01:05:35,563 --> 01:05:37,916
otherwise I'm going to go and complain to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

986
01:05:38,217 --> 01:05:39,420
That's how serious he took it.

987
01:05:39,564 --> 01:05:43,353
Because he doesn't want to face Allah on the Day of Judgment owing anything to anyone.

988
01:05:44,183 --> 01:05:50,036
He wants to be clean, he doesn't want to have in the heart of anyone hard feelings towards him.

989
01:05:50,461 --> 01:05:51,777
So he told them go back.

990
01:05:52,110 --> 01:05:55,829
Come on, and respond back to me otherwise I'm gonna go and complain to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

991
01:05:55,853 --> 01:05:57,105
He said: I'm not gonna respond back to you

992
01:05:59,263 --> 01:06:02,291
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه angrily left.

993
01:06:03,889 --> 01:06:09,068
and he was going to Rasool Allah ﷺ, Rabiah(ربيعة) said: I followed him.

994
01:06:10,018 --> 01:06:14,127
But then, some men from my tribe, clan Aslam(أسلم) came to me and said;

995
01:06:14,748 --> 01:06:19,780
Why is he, going to complain about you, when he is the one

996
01:06:19,804 --> 01:06:21,919
who spoke ill about you in the first place?

997
01:06:23,020 --> 01:06:24,409
Why is he going to complain about you?

998
01:06:24,718 --> 01:06:27,168
Rabiah(ربيعة) said: Do you know, who he is?

999
01:06:28,086 --> 01:06:30,846
This is Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, the second of two.

1000
01:06:31,663 --> 01:06:33,359
He comes second after Rasool Allah ﷺ

1001
01:06:34,793 --> 01:06:37,767
and I don't want him to see you gathering around me

1002
01:06:37,792 --> 01:06:40,063
otherwise he's gonna think that we're ganging up against him.

1003
01:06:41,044 --> 01:06:44,793
And if he gets upset than Rasool Allah ﷺ will become upset

1004
01:06:45,437 --> 01:06:50,106
and if Rasool Allah ﷺ becomes upset, then Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will have His wrath on me

1005
01:06:50,130 --> 01:06:51,354
and that will be the end of Rabiah(ربيعة).

1006
01:06:53,491 --> 01:06:55,148
Get away from me! Go away!

1007
01:06:56,093 --> 01:07:00,248
 Rabiah رضي الله عنه knows who Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is.

1008
01:07:01,814 --> 01:07:05,555
He didn't want Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to even see these people gathering around him

1009
01:07:05,625 --> 01:07:08,318
because he might interpret that they coming to give him support.

1010
01:07:09,088 --> 01:07:13,343
And even though Rabiah(ربيعة) knew that it was Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) who spoke ill about him.

1011
01:07:14,329 --> 01:07:19,270
He still refused to reply, and he also refused to get the assistance of his family.

1012
01:07:19,555 --> 01:07:20,634
He said: Leave me alone!

1013
01:07:21,761 --> 01:07:24,597
And then he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was sitting next to him.

1014
01:07:26,203 --> 01:07:30,039
Rabiah(ربيعة) says: Rasool Allah ﷺ was sitting so he looked up at me and said;

1015
01:07:30,746 --> 01:07:33,015
يا ربيعة ما لك والصديق

1016
01:07:33,246 --> 01:07:36,039
O Rabiah(ربيعة), what's your issue with As-Siddique(ألصديق)?

1017
01:07:36,442 --> 01:07:40,018
The Siddique(ألصديق), that was the name Rasool Allah ﷺ would call him, As-Siddique(ألصديق)

1018
01:07:40,315 --> 01:07:42,754
What's your issue with Siddique(ألصديق).?

1019
01:07:43,495 --> 01:07:47,586
Rabiah(ربيعة) said: O Messenger of Allah, we had this argument

1020
01:07:48,360 --> 01:07:49,656
because of such and such.

1021
01:07:51,489 --> 01:07:55,565
And he said something to me that upset me.

1022
01:07:56,210 --> 01:07:58,861
And then he told me, to answer back and I refused

1023
01:07:59,826 --> 01:08:00,839
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

1024
01:08:00,879 --> 01:08:01,637
أجل

1025
01:08:02,286 --> 01:08:05,468
Yes! Do not respond back to him but say

1026
01:08:05,820 --> 01:08:07,506
O Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), May Allah forgive you!

1027
01:08:08,018 --> 01:08:09,815
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said: You did the right thing.

1028
01:08:10,131 --> 01:08:13,690
You should not respond back to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

1029
01:08:14,296 --> 01:08:16,318
even if he commits wrong against you.

1030
01:08:16,471 --> 01:08:22,159
Don't reply, don't respond back! Rather, you should say;

1031
01:08:22,183 --> 01:08:23,496
May Allah forgive you!

1032
01:08:23,750 --> 01:08:25,961
Not only that, not only should you be quiet

1033
01:08:25,985 --> 01:08:29,161
but you need to make Dua(دُعَا) that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ forgives Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

1034
01:08:30,594 --> 01:08:33,073
That's how much love Rasool Allah ﷺ had to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

1035
01:08:33,304 --> 01:08:35,700
and that's how much gratitude, he had towards him.

1036
01:08:37,024 --> 01:08:42,893
Rasool Allah ﷺ would show extreme loyalty to the ones who were with him from day one.

1037
01:08:44,533 --> 01:08:49,715
And Rasool Allah ﷺ later on, when he opened Makkah all of these great politicians,

1038
01:08:50,088 --> 01:08:57,358
who everybody at that time would want to be close to and have relationship with like, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان)

1039
01:08:57,382 --> 01:09:04,017
and all of the other great men of Arabia at the time in terms of their status and nobility among the people

1040
01:09:04,581 --> 01:09:10,621
but Rasool Allah ﷺ would consider the best to be the ones who came with him from day one, even if they were slaves.

1041
01:09:12,301 --> 01:09:20,190
Rasool Allah ﷺ still remembered the service that they showed to him and to Islam

1042
01:09:20,631 --> 01:09:22,506
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was very grateful for that.

1043
01:09:23,151 --> 01:09:27,364
And that's why Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he felt that he was leaving this world

1044
01:09:29,235 --> 01:09:33,279
when he felt that he is on the doorstep of death.

1045
01:09:34,877 --> 01:09:37,211
He went to the battleground of Uhud(أحَد)

1046
01:09:38,684 --> 01:09:40,936
and he spoke to the Shuhadah(شهداء) of Uhud(أحَد), and said;

1047
01:09:41,854 --> 01:09:44,467
I am going to be your witness on the Day of Judgment

1048
01:09:45,338 --> 01:09:48,431
you gave up your life for the service of this religion.

1049
01:09:49,013 --> 01:09:51,215
I am going to witness for you on the Day of Judgment

1050
01:09:53,016 --> 01:09:55,767
and Rasool Allah ﷺ when he was passing away. He said:

1051
01:09:55,791 --> 01:09:58,984
Close all of the doors of the Masjid(مسجد) except the door of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

1052
01:09:59,009 --> 01:09:59,652
keep it open.

1053
01:10:01,579 --> 01:10:07,403
One day Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه had an argument with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

1054
01:10:08,774 --> 01:10:11,782
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was sitting with the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

1055
01:10:12,831 --> 01:10:15,767
and here comes Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) running

1056
01:10:16,546 --> 01:10:18,069
and the narrator of the Hadith(حديث) said;

1057
01:10:18,577 --> 01:10:23,009
He has lifted his Izaar(إزار) so his knee was uncovered.

1058
01:10:24,576 --> 01:10:27,597
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he saw Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), and he looked at his face. He said:

1059
01:10:27,621 --> 01:10:29,064
أمَّا صاحبكم فقد غامر

1060
01:10:30,680 --> 01:10:35,418
Your friend has been involved in a dispute, I can see it, in his face.

1061
01:10:37,024 --> 01:10:39,290
When Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه came in and he gave Salam(سلام)

1062
01:10:39,314 --> 01:10:42,860
Rasool Allah ﷺ responded and said: What's the problem Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

1063
01:10:43,645 --> 01:10:48,347
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه  said: I had an argument with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

1064
01:10:49,011 --> 01:10:53,749
so I spoke ill about him, but then I regretted that.

1065
01:10:54,589 --> 01:10:58,666
So I told him: O Umar(عُمَر) forgive me, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

1066
01:10:58,691 --> 01:10:59,674
I am not gonna forgive you!

1067
01:11:00,920 --> 01:11:03,672
I told Umar(عُمَر), O Umar(عُمَر) forgive me. He refused and he left.

1068
01:11:05,825 --> 01:11:08,760
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he regreted that.

1069
01:11:09,757 --> 01:11:11,090
So he went to the house of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

1070
01:11:11,114 --> 01:11:13,871
you can see the Sahabah(صحابه), are very fast in forgiving

1071
01:11:15,101 --> 01:11:17,238
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he went to the house of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and said;

1072
01:11:17,278 --> 01:11:18,066
أثمَّ ابوبكر

1073
01:11:18,182 --> 01:11:20,316
Is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) there.? They said: No!

1074
01:11:20,859 --> 01:11:22,617
So he knew that he is gonna be with Rasool Allah ﷺ

1075
01:11:22,641 --> 01:11:26,062
so he went there, and when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was coming

1076
01:11:27,855 --> 01:11:31,790
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه saw that the face of Rasool Allah ﷺ changed

1077
01:11:32,013 --> 01:11:33,003
ثمعارة وجه

1078
01:11:34,179 --> 01:11:36,918
You could tell when Rasool Allah ﷺ is angry and upset

1079
01:11:37,367 --> 01:11:39,502
his facial expressions would change.

1080
01:11:40,224 --> 01:11:41,685
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said;

1081
01:11:42,029 --> 01:11:42,850
فأشفكت

1082
01:11:42,980 --> 01:11:45,136
I felt sorry for Umar(عُمَر)

1083
01:11:46,593 --> 01:11:48,470
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was now worried

1084
01:11:48,974 --> 01:11:52,719
that Rasool Allah ﷺ would be upset with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

1085
01:11:54,121 --> 01:11:57,970
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) he went down on his knees and he said;

1086
01:11:57,995 --> 01:12:01,483
O Rasool Ullah: I am the one, who transgressed against him

1087
01:12:02,081 --> 01:12:05,087
because Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) felt that Rasool Allah ﷺ was angry

1088
01:12:05,373 --> 01:12:07,685
and this anger was directed at Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

1089
01:12:08,392 --> 01:12:12,439
So he wanted to make it clear that it was his fault in the first place.

1090
01:12:12,756 --> 01:12:15,055
He is the one who spoke ill against Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

1091
01:12:15,496 --> 01:12:18,304
But even though Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) mentioned that twice

1092
01:12:18,329 --> 01:12:23,887
and clarify the situation, Rasool Allah ﷺ his facial expressions were still angry.

1093
01:12:24,750 --> 01:12:30,449
And he said: When I came to you, you said that I am a liar

1094
01:12:30,820 --> 01:12:33,645
and Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said that you are telling the truth.

1095
01:12:34,219 --> 01:12:37,378
And he consoled me with his self, and his wealth

1096
01:12:37,671 --> 01:12:39,617
so are you going to keep my friend alone.

1097
01:12:40,652 --> 01:12:43,480
Are you going to keep my friend alone and he said it twice.

1098
01:12:43,765 --> 01:12:46,271
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to make it clear to the Sahabah(صحابه).

1099
01:12:47,244 --> 01:12:50,329
Do not harm Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

1100
01:12:50,670 --> 01:12:52,202
He's the greatest among you!

1101
01:12:52,644 --> 01:12:54,266
Leave them alone and don't harm him.

1102
01:12:54,512 --> 01:12:56,504
Because I'm going to stand for his defense

1103
01:12:57,101 --> 01:12:58,308
I'm going to be on the side.

1104
01:12:59,229 --> 01:13:00,376
The narrator of this Hadith(حديث) said;

1105
01:13:00,416 --> 01:13:04,978
We never saw anybody after that daring to cause any harm to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

1106
01:13:06,628 --> 01:13:09,460
We left him alone. This was in Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ).

1107
01:13:11,109 --> 01:13:14,115
وصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

